Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.00,0:00:12.07,Default,,0,0,0,,﻿1
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.32,0:00:35.70,Default,,0,0,0,,WOMAN: Raindrops on roses
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.78,0:00:39.20,Default,,0,0,0,,And whiskers on kittens
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.62,0:00:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Bright copper kettles
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.38,0:00:45.92,Default,,0,0,0,,And warm woolen mittens
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.38,0:00:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Brown paper packages
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.76,0:00:51.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Tied up with strings
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.09,0:00:54.55,Default,,0,0,0,,These are a few
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.64,0:00:59.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Of my favorite things
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.81,0:01:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: We were\Nsomewhere around Barstow,\Non the edge of the desert,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.23,0:01:07.98,Default,,0,0,0,,when the drugs\Nbegan to take hold.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.07,0:01:10.82,Default,,0,0,0,,(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING\NON CAR STEREO)
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.33,0:01:23.75,Default,,0,0,0,,l remember saying\Nsomething like...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.83,0:01:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel a bit lightheaded.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.50,0:01:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,(EXCLAIMING)\NMaybe you should drive.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.34,0:01:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,(BATS SCREECHING)
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.01,0:01:33.76,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: SuddenIy\Nthere was a terrible roar\Nall around us.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.84,0:01:36.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And the sky was full of\Nwhat looked like huge bats.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.51,0:01:39.64,Default,,0,0,0,,All swooping and screeching\Nand diving around the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.72,0:01:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,And a voice was screaming...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.85,0:01:42.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Holy Jesus! What are\Nthese goddamn animals?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.94,0:01:43.94,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTING)
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.02,0:01:45.56,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Come on, baby
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.94,0:01:48.65,Default,,0,0,0,,You say something?\NHmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.36,0:01:50.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.94,0:01:52.36,Default,,0,0,0,,It's your turn to drive.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.28,0:01:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: No point\Nin mentioning these bats,\Nl thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.66,0:01:57.91,Default,,0,0,0,,The poor bastard'll\Nsee them soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.74,0:02:00.79,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Baby,\Nl'm starting to feel human
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.87,0:02:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Ohh, ohh, yeah
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.50,0:02:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, hey, feel with me, baby
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.71,0:02:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,'Cause l feel it coming on
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.50,0:02:12.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Fucking pigs! Flying !
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.72,0:02:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.43,0:02:19.35,Default,,0,0,0,,We had 2 bags of grass,\N75 pellets of mescaline,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.43,0:02:22.01,Default,,0,0,0,,5 sheets of\Nhigh-powered blotter acid,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.10,0:02:24.35,Default,,0,0,0,,a salt shaker\Nhalf full of cocaine,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.56,0:02:28.56,Default,,0,0,0,,a whole galaxy of\Nmulticolored uppers, downers,\Nscreamers, laughers.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.65,0:02:31.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Also, a quart of tequila,\Na quart of rum,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.40,0:02:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,a case of beer,\Na pint of raw ether...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.11,0:02:34.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.19,0:02:35.86,Default,,0,0,0,,2 dozen amyls.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.24,0:02:38.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Not that we needed\Nall that for the trip,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.49,0:02:41.12,Default,,0,0,0,,but once you get locked\Ninto a serious\Ndrug collection,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.20,0:02:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,the tendency is to\Npush it as far as you can.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.08,0:02:47.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The only thing\Nthat really worried me\Nwas the ether.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.67,0:02:49.50,Default,,0,0,0,,There is nothing\Nin the world more helpless
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.59,0:02:51.67,Default,,0,0,0,,and irresponsible\Nand depraved
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.75,0:02:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,than a man in the depths\Nof an ether binge,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.72,0:02:57.22,Default,,0,0,0,,and l knew\Nwe'd get into that\Nrotten stuff pretty soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.30,0:02:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,WOMAN ON RADIO: A House\Nsubcommittee report says,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.30,0:03:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,illegal drugs killed\N1 60 American Gls last year,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.52,0:03:05.68,Default,,0,0,0,,40 of them in Vietnam.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.77,0:03:07.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Drugs...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.10,0:03:08.35,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING)\NOne toke over the line\NSweet Jesus
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.44,0:03:09.94,Default,,0,0,0,,One toke, man !
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.36,0:03:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,One toke over the line!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.99,0:03:16.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Sitting downtown\Nat a railway station
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.86,0:03:19.57,Default,,0,0,0,,One toke over the line!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.66,0:03:21.20,Default,,0,0,0,,One toke, you poor fool?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.28,0:03:22.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Sweet, sweet Mary!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.37,0:03:24.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait'll you see those\Ngoddamned bats, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.46,0:03:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Mine!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.04,0:03:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,One toke over the line
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.09,0:03:33.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's give that boy a lift.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.67,0:03:35.17,Default,,0,0,0,,What? No!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.42,0:03:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait! We can't stop here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.47,0:03:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,This is bat country.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.06,0:03:47.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Hot damn ! I never rode\Nin a convertible before!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.48,0:03:51.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that right? Well, I guess\Nyou're about ready then,\Naren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.15,0:03:52.56,Default,,0,0,0,,We're your friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.65,0:03:54.23,Default,,0,0,0,,We're not like the others,\Nman. Really.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.32,0:03:57.03,Default,,0,0,0,,No more of that talk\Nor I'll put the fucking\Nleeches on you. Understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.11,0:03:59.07,Default,,0,0,0,,(GONZO GIGGLING)
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.24,0:04:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Get in.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.08,0:04:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: How Iong\Ncould we maintain, l wondered.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.83,0:04:12.17,Default,,0,0,0,,How long before\None of us starts raving\Nand jabbering at this boy?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.50,0:04:14.09,Default,,0,0,0,,What will he think then?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.63,0:04:17.84,Default,,0,0,0,,This same lonely desert\Nwas the last known home\Nof the Manson family.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.51,0:04:19.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Would he make\Nthat grim connection
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.88,0:04:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,when my attorney starts\Nscreaming about bats
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.68,0:04:23.85,Default,,0,0,0,,and huge manta rays\Ncoming down on the car?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.51,0:04:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,lf so, well, we'll just\Nhave to cut his head off\Nand bury him somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.02,0:04:32.02,Default,,0,0,0,,'Cause it goes without saying\Nthat we can't turn him loose.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.52,0:04:33.69,Default,,0,0,0,,He'd report us at once
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.77,0:04:35.90,Default,,0,0,0,,to some kind of outback\NNazi law enforcement agency
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.98,0:04:38.44,Default,,0,0,0,,and they'll run us down\Nlike dogs.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.90,0:04:41.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Jesus, did l say that,\Nor just think it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.82,0:04:44.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Was l talking?\NDid they hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.87,0:04:45.95,Default,,0,0,0,,It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.04,0:04:47.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Just admiring\Nthe shape of your skull.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.100,0:04:48.100,Default,,0,0,0,,BOY: No, thanks!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.08,0:04:51.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe l'd better have a chat\Nwith this boy, l thought.\NI have asthma!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.62,0:04:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps if l explain things,\Nhe'll rest easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.92,0:04:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.55,0:04:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,There's one thing you should\Nprobably understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.01,0:05:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.55,0:05:01.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.68,0:05:04.93,Default,,0,0,0,,(EXCLAIMS)\NI want you to have\Nall the background.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.01,0:05:06.97,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a very\Nominous assignment
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.06,0:05:09.22,Default,,0,0,0,,with overtones\Nof extreme personal danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.52,0:05:11.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a Doctor of Journalism,\Nman.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.31,0:05:13.56,Default,,0,0,0,,This is important,\Ngoddamn it!\NThis is a fucking true story!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.65,0:05:16.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit! Hey, what're you doing?\NSit down. Get the fuck. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.32,0:05:19.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Get your hands\Noff my fucking head !
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.74,0:05:20.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, now, now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.86,0:05:23.53,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: Our vibrations\Nwere getting nasty, but why?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.03,0:05:25.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Was there no communication\Nin this car?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.58,0:05:29.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Had we deteriorated\Nto the level of dumb beasts?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.12,0:05:31.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to understand\Nthat this man at the wheel\Nis my attorney.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.87,0:05:33.83,Default,,0,0,0,,He's not just some dingbat\NI found on the Strip, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.92,0:05:35.33,Default,,0,0,0,,He's a foreigner.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.42,0:05:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I think he's probably Samoan.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.13,0:05:38.88,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't matter,\Nthough, does it?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.50,0:05:40.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you prejudiced?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.59,0:05:41.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.67,0:05:43.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't think so.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.51,0:05:46.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Because in spite of his race,\Nthis man is extremely valuable\Nto me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.97,0:05:49.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, shit.\NI forgot about the beer.\NYou want some?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.39,0:05:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.43,0:05:51.60,Default,,0,0,0,,How about some ether?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.81,0:05:52.85,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.94,0:05:56.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind.\NAll right, let's get right\Nto the heart of this thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.77,0:05:58.02,Default,,0,0,0,,24 hours ago\Nwe were sitting. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.11,0:06:00.86,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\N...in the Pogo Lounge\Nof the Beverly Heights Hotel.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.94,0:06:02.82,Default,,0,0,0,,ln the patio section,\Nof course.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.11,0:06:06.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Drinking Singapore Slings\Nwith mescal on the side.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.62,0:06:10.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Hiding from\Nthe brutish realities of\Nthis foul year of our Lord,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.100,0:06:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,1 971 .
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.46,0:06:14.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Cops were going apeshit. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.87,0:06:15.100,Default,,0,0,0,,(MUTTERING)
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.08,0:06:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps this is the call\Nyou've been waiting\Nfor all this time, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.09,0:06:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.51,0:06:23.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.80,0:06:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.80,0:06:27.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm. Really?\NAll right. Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.26,0:06:30.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah, yeah.\NOh, yeah. Okay. Bye.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.39,0:06:33.14,Default,,0,0,0,,That was headquarters.\NThey want me to. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.23,0:06:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,(CLEARS THROAT)
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.81,0:06:38.06,Default,,0,0,0,,(COINS CLATTERING)
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.15,0:06:39.31,Default,,0,0,0,,(WHISPERING) Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.19,0:06:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,They want me to go\Nto Las Vegas at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.90,0:06:46.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Make contact with\Na Portuguese photographer\Nnamed Lacerda.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.57,0:06:48.41,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll have all the details.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.66,0:06:51.79,Default,,0,0,0,,All I have to do\Nis check into my\Nsoundproof suite.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.08,0:06:53.87,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll seek me out.\NWhat do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.95,0:06:55.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds like real trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.04,0:06:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna need\Nplenty of legal advice\Nbefore this thing is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.42,0:07:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.55,0:07:01.71,Default,,0,0,0,,As your attorney,\NI advise you
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.80,0:07:03.42,Default,,0,0,0,,to rent a very fast car\Nwith no top.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.38,0:07:06.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And you'll need the cocaine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.72,0:07:08.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Tape recorder\Nfor special music.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.60,0:07:11.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Acapulco shirts.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.51,0:07:14.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Get the hell out of L.A.\Nfor at least 48 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.23,0:07:17.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Blows my weekend.\NWhy?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.52,0:07:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,'Cause, naturally,\NI'm gonna have\Nto go with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.23,0:07:24.44,Default,,0,0,0,,And we're gonna have to\Narm ourselves to the teeth.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.53,0:07:26.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.65,0:07:31.24,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean,\Nif a thing's worth doing,\Nit's worth doing right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.87,0:07:34.49,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the American Dream\Nin action.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.50,0:07:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.38,0:07:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit, we'd be fools not to\Nride this strange torpedo\Nall the way out to the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.46,0:07:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed. We must do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.34,0:07:47.72,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of story\Nis this?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.88,0:07:49.30,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the Mint 400.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.38,0:07:51.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The richest off-road race\Nfor motorcycles\Nand dune buggies
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.85,0:07:53.68,Default,,0,0,0,,in the history\Nof organized sport.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.22,0:07:57.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a fantastic spectacle\Nin honor of some\Nfatback grosero,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.39,0:08:00.31,Default,,0,0,0,,who owns\Nthe luxurious Mint Hotel\Nin downtown Las Vegas.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.40,0:08:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,At least that's what\Nthe press release says,\Nanyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.44,0:08:05.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, as your attorney,\NI advise you to buy\Na motorcycle.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.61,0:08:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,How else can you cover\Na thing like this righteously?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.15,0:08:11.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, we're gonna have to\Ndrum it up on our own.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.24,0:08:14.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Pure Gonzo journalism.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.62,0:08:17.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.75,0:08:21.17,Default,,0,0,0,,(TIRES SQUEALING)
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.50,0:08:27.67,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: Getting\Nhold of the drugs and shirts\Nhad been no problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.76,0:08:30.22,Default,,0,0,0,,But the car and tape recorder\Nwere not easy things\Nto round up
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.30,0:08:32.68,Default,,0,0,0,,at 6:30 on a Friday afternoon\Nin Hollywood.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.76,0:08:34.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.14,0:08:36.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Great. Hang on to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.43,0:08:39.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Fucking A,\Nthe gentleman has\Na major credit card !
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.94,0:08:42.52,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right, man.\NDon't take any guff\Nfrom these fucking swine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.61,0:08:43.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I just got through\Nsaying that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.77,0:08:45.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you realize\Nwho the fuck\Nyou're talking to?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.44,0:08:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.\NDo you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.40,0:08:51.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Be over in 30 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.28,0:08:55.70,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE: We're gonna\Nneed a sound store.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.78,0:08:57.95,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: We won't\Nmake the nut unless\Nwe have unlimited credit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.04,0:08:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE: Jesus Christ.\NWe will, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.21,0:09:02.04,Default,,0,0,0,,You Samoans\Nare all the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.12,0:09:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,You have no faith\Nin the essential decency\Nof the white man's culture.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.96,0:09:08.63,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NThe store was closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.71,0:09:10.97,Default,,0,0,0,,But the salesman said\Nhe could wait if we hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.09,0:09:12.47,Default,,0,0,0,,(SIRENS WAILING)
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.55,0:09:13.88,Default,,0,0,0,,But we were\Ndelayed en route
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.97,0:09:16.05,Default,,0,0,0,,when a Stingray in front of us\Nkilled a pedestrian.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.47,0:09:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,We had trouble again\Nwith the car rental agency.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.77,0:09:22.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Mr. Duke,\Nwe're all settled.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.64,0:09:25.06,Default,,0,0,0,,If I could just\Nget your John Hancock,\Nyou're on your way.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.15,0:09:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.65,0:09:28.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen,\Nyou're gonna be real\Ncareful with this car, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.99,0:09:30.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah, man. Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.24,0:09:31.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. Jeez. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.82,0:09:33.74,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.28,0:09:38.45,Default,,0,0,0,,(PANTING)
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.54,0:09:40.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Holy smokes!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.12,0:09:42.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You just backed over\Na two-foot concrete abutment,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.50,0:09:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,you didn't even slow down.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.83,0:09:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,What were you going about,\NI don't know,\N45 miles an hour backwards?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.75,0:09:48.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey.\NThere's no harm done.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.46,0:09:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh?\NI always test\Nthe transmission that way,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.17,0:09:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,the rear end\Nfor stress factors.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.34,0:09:53.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, this is really\Na nice pen, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.17,0:09:54.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, listen, you. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.84,0:09:57.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You fellows haven't\Nbeen drinking, have you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.43,0:09:59.31,Default,,0,0,0,,No. Not me.\NOh.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.39,0:10:00.64,Default,,0,0,0,,We're responsible people.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.73,0:10:01.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, hey, hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.02,0:10:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn it,\Nyou've got my pen !
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.23,0:10:06.27,Default,,0,0,0,,(TIRES SCREECHING)
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.36,0:10:08.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn hippies!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.90,0:10:12.24,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: We spent\Nthe rest of that night
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.32,0:10:14.03,Default,,0,0,0,,rounding up materials\Nand packing the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.57,0:10:17.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we ate some mescaline\Nand went swimming.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.41,0:10:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Our trip was different.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.33,0:10:23.66,Default,,0,0,0,,lt was to be\Na classic affirmation
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.75,0:10:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,of everything right and true\Nin the national character.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.25,0:10:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,A gross physical salute\Nto the fantastic possibilities\Nof life in this country.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.71,0:10:32.50,Default,,0,0,0,,But only for those\Nwith true grit.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.59,0:10:34.51,Default,,0,0,0,,And we are chock\Nfull of that, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.38,0:10:36.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn right!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.47,0:10:40.72,Default,,0,0,0,,My attorney\Nunderstands this concept,\Ndespite his racial handicap.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.31,0:10:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,But do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.64,0:10:43.64,Default,,0,0,0,,(GIGGLING)
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.73,0:10:47.56,Default,,0,0,0,,He said he understood,\Nbut l could see in his eyes\Nthat he didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.90,0:10:49.23,Default,,0,0,0,,He was lying to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.32,0:10:50.73,Default,,0,0,0,,(GONZO SCREAMING)
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.41,0:11:05.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Medicine!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.54,0:11:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What?\NMedicine!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.04,0:11:08.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Medicine?\NOh, yeah, medicine. Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.58,0:11:09.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.71,0:11:12.38,Default,,0,0,0,,(SHRIEKING)\NDon't worry.\NThis man has a bad heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.63,0:11:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Angina pectoris.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.26,0:11:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,But we have a cure for it.\NHere you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.26,0:11:17.72,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.80,0:11:20.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Big whiff. Big whiff.\NBig whiff, sonny boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.05,0:11:23.10,Default,,0,0,0,,There you go. Much better.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.64,0:11:24.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Now for the doctor.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.27,0:11:27.06,Default,,0,0,0,,(GROANING)
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.40,0:11:32.44,Default,,0,0,0,,(SQUEALING)
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.03,0:11:40.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What the. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.03,0:11:44.54,Default,,0,0,0,,What the fuck\Nare we doing out here\Nin the middle of the desert?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.04,0:11:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Somebody call the police.\NWe need help.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.100,0:11:48.04,Default,,0,0,0,,We need help.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.12,0:11:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,We need help. We need help.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.46,0:11:51.46,Default,,0,0,0,,(HORN HONKS)
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.92,0:11:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,(LAUGHING)
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.38,0:12:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.93,0:12:03.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Truth?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.47,0:12:05.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, we're going to Vegas. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.81,0:12:06.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Vegas.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.98,0:12:10.56,Default,,0,0,0,,To croak a scag baron\Nnamed Savage Henry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.65,0:12:11.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.73,0:12:15.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Why? Because I've\Nknown him for years\Nbut he ripped us off.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.40,0:12:17.40,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE: And you know\Nwhat that means.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.49,0:12:19.24,Default,,0,0,0,,And you know what that means.\NRight?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.32,0:12:20.32,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.41,0:12:23.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Savage Henry\Nhas cashed his check.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.49,0:12:25.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Cashed his check.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.91,0:12:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,And we're gonna\Nrip his lungs out.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.16,0:12:30.100,Default,,0,0,0,,That bastard won't\Nget away with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.08,0:12:34.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, what is\Ngoing on in this country\Nwhen a scum sucker like that
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.67,0:12:36.75,Default,,0,0,0,,can get away\Nwith sandbagging\Na Doctor of Journalism?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.84,0:12:37.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you tell me that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.63,0:12:41.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!\NThanks for the ride!\NI like you guys!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.09,0:12:43.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Really, don't worry about me!\NWait a minute!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.10,0:12:44.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Come back and have a beer!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.60,0:12:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit. Fuck.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.14,0:12:49.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna miss him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.60,0:12:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Move over.\NDid you see his eyes?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.44,0:12:54.77,Default,,0,0,0,,We have to get\Nout of California\Nbefore that kid finds a cop.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.94,0:12:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,(CACKLING)\NCome on.\NScoot over, you fat bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.90,0:12:58.61,Default,,0,0,0,,We had a real freak\Non our hands!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.69,0:13:00.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, shit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.82,0:13:06.66,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: It was\Nabsolutely imperative that\Nwe get to the Mint Hotel
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.74,0:13:08.66,Default,,0,0,0,,before the deadline\Nfor press registration.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.75,0:13:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise we might\Nhave to pay for our suite.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.46,0:13:16.96,Default,,0,0,0,,(SCREECHING)
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.71,0:13:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Jesus!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.47,0:13:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you see what God\Njust did to us, man?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.01,0:13:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,God didn't do that.\NYou did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.55,0:13:26.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You're a fucking\Nnarcotics agent.\NI knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.93,0:13:28.68,Default,,0,0,0,,That was our cocaine,\Nyou pig !
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.77,0:13:30.48,Default,,0,0,0,,You fucking pig, swine, whore!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.56,0:13:31.68,Default,,0,0,0,,You better be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.52,0:13:36.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Plenty of vultures out here\Nthat'll pick your bones\Nclean before morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.57,0:13:38.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You fucking whore.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.19,0:13:39.94,Default,,0,0,0,,(FEIGNING LAUGHTER)
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.61,0:13:43.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's your half\Nof the sunshine acid. Eat it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.57,0:13:44.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.78,0:13:46.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Great.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.28,0:13:49.99,Default,,0,0,0,,How long do I have?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.08,0:13:52.04,Default,,0,0,0,,As your attorney,\NI advise you to drive\Nat top speed
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.12,0:13:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,or it'll be a goddamn\Nmiracle if we can get there
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.50,0:13:56.75,Default,,0,0,0,,before you turn\Ninto a wild animal.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.96,0:13:58.71,Default,,0,0,0,,(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.84,0:14:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,(MUTTERING)
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.76,0:14:02.38,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Yeah, yeah
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.72,0:14:03.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you ready for that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.80,0:14:06.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Checking into a Vegas hotel\Nunder a phony name
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.60,0:14:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,with intent to\Ncommit capital fraud\Nand a head full of acid?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.77,0:14:12.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I sure hope so.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.68,0:14:14.10,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: 30 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.19,0:14:15.85,Default,,0,0,0,,lt was going to be very close.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.03,0:14:22.94,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) WeII,\Nshe's all you'd ever want
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.03,0:14:24.78,Default,,0,0,0,,She's the kind\Nl'd like to flaunt
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.86,0:14:26.57,Default,,0,0,0,,And take to dinner
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.74,0:14:29.03,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN ON P.A. : WeIcome\Nto the Mint Hotel!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.12,0:14:30.74,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) WeII,\Nshe always knows her place
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.83,0:14:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,She's got style\NShe's got grace
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.12,0:14:34.83,Default,,0,0,0,,She's a winner
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.96,0:14:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,(HORN HONKING)
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.71,0:14:38.46,Default,,0,0,0,,She's a lady
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.42,0:14:41.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa, whoa, whoa
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.17,0:14:42.55,Default,,0,0,0,,She's a lady
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.63,0:14:43.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm? Mmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.88,0:14:46.97,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) TaIking about\Nmy little lady
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.09,0:14:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN: Come on, take the ticket.\NWe're busy here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.01,0:14:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) And the Iady is mine
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.22,0:14:52.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, take the ticket.\NTake it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.31,0:14:53.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Take the ticket.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.19,0:14:57.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I need this, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.81,0:14:59.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll remember your face.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.48,0:15:04.40,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: There is\Nno way of explaining\Nthe terror l felt.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.16,0:15:10.16,Default,,0,0,0,,WOMAN ON P.A. : Attention,\Nall Mint Hotel guests.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.24,0:15:12.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Will the owner\Nof a green Pinto
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.79,0:15:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Minnesota license plate\NTG0432...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.50,0:15:18.29,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\Nl was pouring sweat.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.58,0:15:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,My blood is too thick\Nfor Nevada.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.34,0:15:24.09,Default,,0,0,0,,l've never been able\Nto properly explain myself\Nin this climate.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.17,0:15:25.26,Default,,0,0,0,,(MAN CHATTERING)
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.34,0:15:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. Be quiet, be calm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.93,0:15:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Name, rank\Nand press affiliation.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.56,0:15:34.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing else.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.64,0:15:37.60,Default,,0,0,0,,. . .hamburger stand.\NShe was a waitress\Nabout 1 6 years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.69,0:15:40.36,Default,,0,0,0,,They chopped her goddamn\Nhead off right there\Nin the parking lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.44,0:15:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Then they cut all\Nkinds of holes in her\Nand sucked out the blood.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.57,0:15:45.65,Default,,0,0,0,,They were after\Nthe pineal gland, I think.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.74,0:15:46.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.07,0:15:48.36,Default,,0,0,0,,No. How's your mama?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.45,0:15:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,lgnore this terrible drug.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.87,0:15:52.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.45,0:15:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Pretend it's not happening.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.75,0:15:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTS)
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.87,0:15:57.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi there!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.08,0:16:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,My name?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.17,0:16:05.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Raoul Duke!\NOn the list. Freelance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.84,0:16:07.22,Default,,0,0,0,,On the list, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.30,0:16:08.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Total coverage.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.72,0:16:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I have my attorney. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.77,0:16:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,With me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.10,0:16:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,And I realize that his name\Nis not on that list.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.11,0:16:23.65,Default,,0,0,0,,But we must have that suite!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.73,0:16:25.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, we must have that suite.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.65,0:16:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the score here?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.86,0:16:30.28,Default,,0,0,0,,What's next?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.57,0:16:32.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Your suite isn't ready yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.74,0:16:35.58,Default,,0,0,0,,But someone\Nwas looking for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.20,0:16:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,No! We haven't done\Nanything yet! Move!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.16,0:16:39.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I can handle this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.92,0:16:43.33,Default,,0,0,0,,This man suffers\Nfrom a bad heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.42,0:16:46.04,Default,,0,0,0,,But I have\Nplenty of medicine.\NMy name is Dr. Gonzo.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.13,0:16:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare our suite at once.\NWe'll be in the bar.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.72,0:16:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTS)
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.65,0:17:06.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know about you,\Nbut I'm starting\Nto feel that drink.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.57,0:17:07.73,Default,,0,0,0,,(CHUCKLING)
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.28,0:17:10.28,Default,,0,0,0,,(GROWLS)
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.99,0:17:13.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, beat it.\NBeat it. Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.78,0:17:17.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I like the way\Nyou did that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.95,0:17:18.91,Default,,0,0,0,,(EXCLAIMS)
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.100,0:17:21.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on. Come on. Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.66,0:17:24.17,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that?\NCome on, come on.\NLet's get some peanuts.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.29,0:17:26.54,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE: Peanuts?\NThat's one thing\Nthat's good for you, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.63,0:17:28.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Peanuts, man.\NJesus!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.38,0:17:30.42,Default,,0,0,0,,2 Cuba Libres, beer\Nand mescal on the side.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.51,0:17:31.92,Default,,0,0,0,,BARTENDER: You got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.30,0:17:35.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll bet you're a Libra.\NMmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.43,0:17:37.81,Default,,0,0,0,,(LAUGHING)
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.93,0:17:40.43,Default,,0,0,0,,(WOMAN MOANING)
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.52,0:17:44.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Who's Lacerda?\NLacerda?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.15,0:17:46.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, he's waiting for us\Non the 1 2th floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.44,0:17:48.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Room 1 250. Lacerda.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.53,0:17:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\Nl couldn't remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.99,0:17:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The name rang a bell,\Nbut l couldn't concentrate.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.20,0:17:57.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Terrible things were happening\Nall around us.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.91,0:17:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,(GURGLING)
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.83,0:18:01.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Buy us some golf shoes,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.50,0:18:03.83,Default,,0,0,0,,otherwise we'll never\Nget out of this place alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.38,0:18:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Impossible to walk\Nin this muck.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.50,0:18:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,No footing at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.67,0:18:16.13,Default,,0,0,0,,WOMAN ON P.A. :\NMr. Roger Pratt, please\Ncall the hotel operator.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.72,0:18:22.27,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) How can I bear\Nto see your heart break?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.23,0:18:25.52,Default,,0,0,0,,To see your heart break
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.60,0:18:27.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Over me
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.86,0:18:35.61,Default,,0,0,0,,(GROWLING)
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.26,0:18:56.47,Default,,0,0,0,,l was right in the middle\Nof a fucking reptile zoo
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.55,0:18:59.26,Default,,0,0,0,,and somebody was giving booze\Nto these goddamn things.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.89,0:19:03.18,Default,,0,0,0,,lt won't be long now\Nbefore they tear us to shreds.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.98,0:19:09.40,Default,,0,0,0,,(MUMBLING INCOHERENTLY)
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.70,0:19:18.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.32,0:19:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell them to get out\Ntheir fucking golf shoes!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.08,0:19:23.08,Default,,0,0,0,,(ALL GASPING)
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.87,0:19:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Jesus God Almighty,\Nlook at that bunch\Nover there, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.50,0:19:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,They've spotted us.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.29,0:19:30.25,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: That's the press table,\Nman.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.42,0:19:32.92,Default,,0,0,0,,We're gonna have to sign in\Nfor our credentials.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.21,0:19:36.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.97,0:19:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you ready?\NHmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.72,0:19:41.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.10,0:19:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, hurry up.\NWait! Wait, wait!\NFucking don't leave me here!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.27,0:19:49.02,Default,,0,0,0,,BOY: Two club sandwiches,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.10,0:19:52.06,Default,,0,0,0,,and 2 more club sandwiches.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.52,0:19:56.44,Default,,0,0,0,,One, two, three, four\Nshrimp cocktails.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.61,0:19:59.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm?\NAnd nine fresh grapefruit.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.57,0:20:01.53,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: Vitamin C.\NNeed all we can get.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.66,0:20:04.91,Default,,0,0,0,,BOY: Four chicken. . .\NDUKE: There's a big\Nmachine in the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.99,0:20:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Some kind of. . .\NQuart of rum.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.95,0:20:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, electric snake\Ncoming straight at us.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.79,0:20:11.25,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: Shoot it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.46,0:20:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Not yet.\NI want to study its habits.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.46,0:20:17.38,Default,,0,0,0,,BOY: You motorcycle people\Nsure are hearty eaters.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.05,0:20:20.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I need the cart. I need\Nto return with the cart.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.55,0:20:23.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, but the cart\Nneeds to go back with. . .\NI'll be back!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.81,0:20:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: You bastard.\NI've been hit, man !
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.85,0:20:28.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I leave you alone\Nfor three minutes
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.14,0:20:29.85,Default,,0,0,0,,and you start\Nwaving that goddamn
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.94,0:20:32.61,Default,,0,0,0,,marlin spike around\Nyelling about reptiles.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.90,0:20:34.19,Default,,0,0,0,,What're you talking about,\Nman?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.27,0:20:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You scared the shit\Nout of those people.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.07,0:20:37.57,Default,,0,0,0,,They were ready\Nto call the cops.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.65,0:20:39.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir, you were lucky\NI came back in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.95,0:20:41.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't come near me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.49,0:20:43.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't come fucking near me!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.62,0:20:45.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Leave me alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.70,0:20:47.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell, the only reason\Nthey gave us press passes
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.50,0:20:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,was to get you\Nout of there, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.62,0:20:51.29,Default,,0,0,0,,(KNOCKING ON DOOR)\NOh, God ! What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.38,0:20:53.83,Default,,0,0,0,,That scene straightened me\Nright out, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.13,0:20:55.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Who's at the door?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.09,0:20:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN ON T.V. : As the bombing\Ncontinues in Laos...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.76,0:21:00.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Just a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.68,0:21:04.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Holy shit. Oh, my God.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.14,0:21:06.93,Default,,0,0,0,,(MAN CONTINUES\NCHATTERING ON T.V.)
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.14,0:21:11.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi. I'm Lacerda,\Nyour photographer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.15,0:21:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Duke?\NDUKE: Mmm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.36,0:21:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Back there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.95,0:21:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Duke?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.82,0:21:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Duke? Hi !
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.32,0:21:25.32,Default,,0,0,0,,(LAUGHS)
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.49,0:21:28.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Lacerda. Your photographer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.29,0:21:29.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not Portuguese, man !
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.91,0:21:32.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, too bad you guys\Nmissed the bikes checking in.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.75,0:21:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, man, what a sight!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.79,0:21:38.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Husquavarnas, Yamahas, DMZs.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.76,0:21:41.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Kawasakis!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.59,0:21:44.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Maicos. Pursang !
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.39,0:21:46.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Swedish Fireballs.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.14,0:21:49.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Couple of Triumphs.\NHere and there a CZ.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.85,0:21:52.27,Default,,0,0,0,,All very, very fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.81,0:21:53.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Very.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.48,0:21:56.56,Default,,0,0,0,,What a race it's gonna be.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.24,0:22:03.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.08,0:22:09.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna let myself out.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.24,0:22:12.29,Default,,0,0,0,,We know what\Nyou're up to, man.\NHmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.47,0:22:25.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna tell you. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.55,0:22:29.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He's lying to us.\NI could see it in his eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.64,0:22:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Eyes?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.72,0:22:33.56,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN ON T.V. : Late\Nbattle reports indicate...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.64,0:22:35.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Panic now, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.44,0:22:38.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Turn this shit off.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.03,0:22:47.11,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: The racers\Nwere ready at dawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.20,0:22:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Very tense.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.95,0:22:53.45,Default,,0,0,0,,ln some circles, the Mint 400\Nis a far, far better thing\Nthan the Super Bowl,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.83,0:22:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,the Kentucky Derby
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.46,0:22:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,and the Lower Oakland\NRoller Derby Finals\Nall rolled into one.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.00,0:22:59.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Slow down !\NThis is a restricted area!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.63,0:23:02.05,Default,,0,0,0,,This race attracts\Na very special breed.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.34,0:23:04.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck off.\NAll right.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.67,0:23:06.80,Default,,0,0,0,,lt was time to get grounded,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.09,0:23:08.72,Default,,0,0,0,,to ponder this\Nrotten assignment
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.80,0:23:10.39,Default,,0,0,0,,and figure out\Nhow to cope with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.47,0:23:11.97,Default,,0,0,0,,lt was time to do the job.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.18,0:23:14.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Those of us\Nwho had been up all night
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.73,0:23:16.56,Default,,0,0,0,,were in no mood\Nfor coffee and donuts.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.23,0:23:19.19,Default,,0,0,0,,We wanted strong drink.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.31,0:23:20.90,Default,,0,0,0,,We were, after all
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.98,0:23:23.19,Default,,0,0,0,,the absolute cream\Nof the national\Nsporting press.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.65,0:23:24.90,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN: Pull !
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.40,0:23:26.95,Default,,0,0,0,,We were gathered here\Nin Las Vegas
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.03,0:23:28.86,Default,,0,0,0,,for this very\Nspecial moment in sport.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.49,0:23:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,When it comes to\Na thing like this,\Nthey don't fool around.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.87,0:23:34.12,Default,,0,0,0,,(SNORING)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.08,0:23:37.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.25,0:23:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Money plays. Money plays.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.63,0:23:45.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Kill the body,\Nthe head will die.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.34,0:23:46.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Ali-Frazier fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.34,0:23:48.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Crazy shit, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.68,0:23:50.05,Default,,0,0,0,,A proper end to the '60s.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.68,0:23:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Ali beaten by\Na human hamburger.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.97,0:23:55.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Both Kennedys\Nmurdered by mutants.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.64,0:23:56.77,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN: Hey, they're starting !
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.85,0:23:58.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, shit, they're starting.\NLet's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.52,0:24:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN ON P.A. :\NLadies and gentlemen,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.44,0:24:05.11,Default,,0,0,0,,welcome to the start\Nof the $50,000 Mint 400\NDesert Race.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.19,0:24:08.45,Default,,0,0,0,,With a purse of $50,000\Ngoing to the winner
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.53,0:24:10.91,Default,,0,0,0,,of this grueling,\Ngut-wrenching, dust-eating,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.03,0:24:13.49,Default,,0,0,0,,in-your-face\Nmotocross extravaganza!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.54,0:24:16.41,Default,,0,0,0,,And away we go!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.50,0:24:18.75,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got\Nrooster tails going!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.83,0:24:21.17,Default,,0,0,0,,We're here to spit\Nin your enemy's eye!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.25,0:24:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,There they go.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.59,0:24:27.09,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, our second group\Nof 1 0 is getting in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.17,0:24:29.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Kawasakis, Triumphs, Maicos.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.05,0:24:31.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we are.\NWe're ready to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.05,0:24:33.93,Default,,0,0,0,,lt's the green flag,\Nand they're off!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.01,0:24:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Another great start\Nwith a lot of dirt\Nhappening on this hill!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.18,0:24:38.98,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, here we go\Nwith the third group.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.06,0:24:40.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And they're off!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:40.90,0:24:44.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we go.\NNumber 45 riding in\Nthe number 4 position
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.57,0:24:47.11,Default,,0,0,0,,is choking as the dust flies!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.19,0:24:50.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd better wet those\Nbandannas you got\Nstretched over your face!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:51.99,0:24:54.91,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: There was\Nsomething like 1 90 more bikes\Nwaiting to start.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.99,0:24:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me a beer, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.08,0:24:57.62,Default,,0,0,0,,They were due to go off,\N1 0 at a time
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.91,0:24:59.87,Default,,0,0,0,,every two minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.08,0:25:02.75,Default,,0,0,0,,BARTENDER: There you go,\Nbuddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.83,0:25:03.83,Default,,0,0,0,,(BLOWING NOSE)
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.25,0:25:09.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn it.\NWhat day is it? Saturday?\NShit.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.97,0:25:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,More like Sunday.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.26,0:25:17.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello! Anyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.18,0:25:20.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you seen the race?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.60,0:25:23.81,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: By 10:00,\Nthey were spread out\Nall over the course.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.27,0:25:26.23,Default,,0,0,0,,lt was no longer a race.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:26.48,0:25:28.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it was\Nan endurance contest.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.57,0:25:31.36,Default,,0,0,0,,The idea of trying\Nto cover this race
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.45,0:25:33.86,Default,,0,0,0,,in any conventional\Npress sense was absurd.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:33.95,0:25:36.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! It's pretty great, huh?\NWhat?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.12,0:25:38.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on in !
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.79,0:25:42.41,Default,,0,0,0,,(SHUTTER CLICKING)
Dialogue: 0,0:25:43.46,0:25:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just gonna try\Ndifferent combinations\Nof lenses and film
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.21,0:25:50.30,Default,,0,0,0,,until I find something\Nthat works in this dust!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:50.55,0:25:52.09,Default,,0,0,0,,(HELICOPTER WHIRRING)
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.34,0:25:53.68,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.76,0:25:54.84,Default,,0,0,0,,(GUNS FIRING)
Dialogue: 0,0:25:54.93,0:25:57.72,Default,,0,0,0,,That's fucking\Nmachine guns, man.\NThey're firing at us.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.81,0:26:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Machine guns.\NIt's a goddamn war zone!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.68,0:26:02.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Get us out of here quick!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.14,0:26:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,(LACERDA WHOOPING)\NQuick, man !
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.73,0:26:05.65,Default,,0,0,0,,We're gonna be killed,\Nfor fuck's sake!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.73,0:26:08.61,Default,,0,0,0,,What the. . .\NOh, no. Oh, God. Oh, God.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.69,0:26:10.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:12.15,0:26:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the damn race?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.70,0:26:16.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Beats me, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.45,0:26:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,We're just good,\Npatriotic Americans\Nlike yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.70,0:26:22.95,Default,,0,0,0,,What outfit you fellows with?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.21,0:26:26.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh. The sporting press.\NWe're friendlies.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.92,0:26:28.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Hired geeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:32.72,0:26:33.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.68,0:26:35.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.01,0:26:37.26,Default,,0,0,0,,(LACERDA WHOOPING)
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.35,0:26:38.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:38.76,0:26:40.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Get him !
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.35,0:26:42.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Freaks.\NTake me back to the pits.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.35,0:26:44.60,Default,,0,0,0,,No! No, no, no.\NWe have to go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.69,0:26:46.64,Default,,0,0,0,,We need total coverage!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.73,0:26:48.19,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\Nlt was time, l felt,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.27,0:26:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,for an agonizing reappraisal\Nof the whole scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.36,0:26:52.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You're fired.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:54.11,0:26:55.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Awful jackass.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.57,0:26:58.91,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.99,0:27:00.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Just drive into the dust!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.37,0:27:01.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I never wanna see you again.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.70,0:27:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Just drive into the dust!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.58,0:27:05.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.46,0:27:07.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh !
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.17,0:27:13.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The race was\Ndefinitely underway.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:13.88,0:27:15.47,Default,,0,0,0,,l had witnessed the start.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.59,0:27:17.22,Default,,0,0,0,,l was sure of that much.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:17.64,0:27:19.14,Default,,0,0,0,,But what now?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:19.72,0:27:21.35,Default,,0,0,0,,What comes next?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:22.77,0:27:25.39,Default,,0,0,0,,(POP MUSIC PLAYING)
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.15,0:27:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Put on the radio.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:30.52,0:27:31.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Turn on the tape machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:31.86,0:27:33.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Roll every\Ngoddamn window down.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.19,0:27:36.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us taste this\Ncool desert wind.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.57,0:27:40.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, yes.\NThis is what it's all about.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.95,0:27:42.66,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NTotal control now.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.24,0:27:45.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Tooling along the main drag\Non a Saturday night in Vegas.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:47.08,0:27:49.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Two good old boys\Nin a fire-apple\Nred convertible.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.34,0:27:52.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Stoned, ripped...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.80,0:27:55.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Twisted, good people.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.76,0:27:58.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Hot fuck.\NThat sounds heavy.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:58.93,0:28:00.97,Default,,0,0,0,,29 cent hot dogs.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.10,0:28:03.89,Default,,0,0,0,,What are we doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.97,0:28:06.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Are we here to\Nentertain ourselves\Nor do the job?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.64,0:28:08.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Do the job, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.39,0:28:09.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.60,0:28:13.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Crab Louie and\Na quart of muscatel for $20.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:15.28,0:28:18.24,Default,,0,0,0,,As your attorney,\NI advise you to drive\Nover to the Tropicana.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.32,0:28:21.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Guy Lombardo.\NHe's in the Blue Room\Nwith his Royal Canadians.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.28,0:28:22.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.41,0:28:23.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Why? Why what?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.29,0:28:28.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Why should I pay\Nmy hard-earned dollars\Nto watch a fucking corpse?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.37,0:28:29.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know about you,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.87,0:28:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,but in my line of business\Nit's important to be hep.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.71,0:28:35.71,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell do you\Nthink you're doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.80,0:28:38.46,Default,,0,0,0,,This is not a parking area!\NYou've got to move your car!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.55,0:28:41.18,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't park your car here.\NExcuse me. Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.26,0:28:42.39,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.47,0:28:43.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't park. . . Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:43.60,0:28:45.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't park your car here!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.22,0:28:46.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.31,0:28:47.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this not\Na reasonable place to park?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.98,0:28:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Reasonable?\NYou're on a sidewalk!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.73,0:28:51.02,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a sidewalk!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.10,0:28:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,This is not a parking area!\NDebbie Reynolds?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:53.02,0:28:54.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't park\Non the sidewalk!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:54.69,0:28:55.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Seems like a hot ticket.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.82,0:28:57.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.11,0:28:59.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Drove all the way from L.A.\Nfor this show.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:00.24,0:29:01.82,Default,,0,0,0,,We're friends of Debbie's.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:02.16,0:29:04.07,Default,,0,0,0,,(ORCHESTRA PLAYING)
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.16,0:29:06.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, bye.\NWe'll see you later.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:06.24,0:29:08.33,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: This was\NBob Hope's turf,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.41,0:29:09.66,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING)\NStrangers in the night
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.75,0:29:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Frank Sinatra's,\NSpiro Agnew's.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.12,0:29:13.71,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Exchanging gIances
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.79,0:29:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The place fairly reeked\Nof high-grade Formica\Nand plastic palm trees.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.17,0:29:21.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Clearly a high-class\Nrefuge for big spenders.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.51,0:29:25.10,Default,,0,0,0,,It's started.\NIs she on stage?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:25.18,0:29:26.68,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN: She is. Sold out.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.77,0:29:29.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, sir.\NFull house. I'm sorry, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.06,0:29:31.93,Default,,0,0,0,,We drove all the way\Nfrom L.A. for this show.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.02,0:29:34.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I said there are\Nno seats left, sir,\Nat any price.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:34.27,0:29:35.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck seats!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.90,0:29:37.40,Default,,0,0,0,,We're friends with Debbie.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.48,0:29:39.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I used to romp with her.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.95,0:29:43.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you prepared\Nto go to court?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.53,0:29:44.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that depends.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.07,0:29:47.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanna talk to you\Nfor a second.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:47.70,0:29:50.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Your attitude constitutes\Na breach of faith.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.96,0:29:53.87,Default,,0,0,0,,In Nevada, that's illegal.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.46,0:29:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.63,0:29:58.63,Default,,0,0,0,,My name? Tony Pizzacata.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.71,0:30:00.67,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: Tony Pizzacata.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:01.22,0:30:03.38,Default,,0,0,0,,TONY: What, may I ask,\Nis your name, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.47,0:30:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: It's on my\Ndriver's license.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.76,0:30:09.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I think we might be able\Nto squeeze you in, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.39,0:30:10.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you kindly.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.56,0:30:12.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll have to\Nstand in the back.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.60,0:30:16.90,Default,,0,0,0,,After a lot of bad noise\Nhe let us in for nothing
Dialogue: 0,0:30:17.57,0:30:20.61,Default,,0,0,0,,provided\Nwe would stand quietly\Nin the back and not smoke.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:20.82,0:30:22.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Excellent.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:22.95,0:30:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,ANNOUNCER:\NLadies and gentlemen,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.24,0:30:27.16,Default,,0,0,0,,the Desert lnn\Nis proud to present\Nthe one, the only,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.24,0:30:30.33,Default,,0,0,0,,the incomparable\NMiss Debbie Reynolds!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:30.58,0:30:32.25,Default,,0,0,0,,(CHORUS SINGING)\NOoh, ooh
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.66,0:30:34.50,Default,,0,0,0,,DEBBIE: Good evening,\Nladies and gentlemen!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.58,0:30:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,lt's wonderful to be here\Nwith all you fabulous people!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:38.75,0:30:41.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's rock and roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:41.59,0:30:43.17,Default,,0,0,0,,(CHORUS SINGING)\NSgt. Pepper's\NLonely Hearts Club Band
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.26,0:30:45.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!\NWhat the hell's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:45.97,0:30:47.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Get them out!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.60,0:30:49.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, get out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.26,0:30:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Get them out.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.43,0:30:52.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Out!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.77,0:30:57.69,Default,,0,0,0,,(DUKE GIGGLING HYSTERICALLY)
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.44,0:31:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit! We wandered into\Na fucking time capsule there.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.74,0:31:08.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Scumbag !
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.32,0:31:12.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll find where you live\Nand burn your house down,\Nyou piece of shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:13.33,0:31:15.12,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened?\NOh.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.66,0:31:18.96,Default,,0,0,0,,One of these days I'll toss\Na fucking bomb in that place.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.80,0:31:24.01,Default,,0,0,0,,(MUSIC PLAYING)
Dialogue: 0,0:31:32.89,0:31:34.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, wait. You see that?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.60,0:31:36.18,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the place, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:36.48,0:31:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll never\Nfuck with us here.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.94,0:31:42.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the ether?\NMescaline's not working.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.57,0:31:43.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.82,0:31:48.91,Default,,0,0,0,,There we go. Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:53.62,0:31:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:57.83,0:31:58.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:00.34,0:32:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,(SNIFFING)
Dialogue: 0,0:32:03.50,0:32:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,(GROANS)
Dialogue: 0,0:32:05.17,0:32:06.59,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: DeviI ether.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:07.63,0:32:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,lt makes you behave\Nlike the village drunkard\Nin some early lrish novel.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:11.18,0:32:13.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Total loss of all\Nbasic motor skills.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.77,0:32:16.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Blurred vision,\Nno balance, numb tongue.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.81,0:32:18.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The mind recoils in horror,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:19.02,0:32:21.52,Default,,0,0,0,,unable to communicate\Nwith the spinal column,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.61,0:32:23.73,Default,,0,0,0,,which is interesting\Nbecause you can\Nactually watch yourself
Dialogue: 0,0:32:23.82,0:32:27.44,Default,,0,0,0,,behaving in this terrible way\Nbut you can't control it.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:31.53,0:32:34.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You approach the turnstiles\Nand know that\Nwhen you get there
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.87,0:32:37.83,Default,,0,0,0,,you have to give the man $2\Nor he won't let you inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.91,0:32:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,But when you get there\Neverything goes wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.71,0:32:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Some angry Rotarian\Nshoves you
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.21,0:32:45.59,Default,,0,0,0,,and you think,\N"What's happening here?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.67,0:32:46.92,Default,,0,0,0,,"What's going on?"
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.01,0:32:48.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And you hear\Nyourself mumbling.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:48.72,0:32:51.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Dogs fucked the Pope.\NNo fault of mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:51.68,0:32:52.89,Default,,0,0,0,,(MUMBLING)
Dialogue: 0,0:32:53.81,0:32:56.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Ether is the perfect drug\Nfor Las Vegas.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.93,0:33:00.06,Default,,0,0,0,,ln this town\Nthey love a drunk.\NFresh meat.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.14,0:33:01.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, buddy. Come on.\NHoly. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.02,0:33:06.07,Default,,0,0,0,,So they put us\Nthrough the turnstiles\Nand turned us loose inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.73,0:33:09.07,Default,,0,0,0,,(DRUM ROLL)\NANNOUNCER:\NLadies and gentlemen,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.15,0:33:11.03,Default,,0,0,0,,boys and girls,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:11.11,0:33:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,visitors of all ages,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:14.41,0:33:18.83,Default,,0,0,0,,the Bazooko Casino Circus\Nproudly presents,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.91,0:33:22.12,Default,,0,0,0,,the Flying Fellinis!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.73,0:33:47.23,Default,,0,0,0,,(WHOOPING)
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.82,0:33:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God !
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.53,0:33:57.70,Default,,0,0,0,,(SNIFFS DEEPLY)
Dialogue: 0,0:34:02.66,0:34:04.12,Default,,0,0,0,,(SNARLING)
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.51,0:34:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.98,0:34:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:30.53,0:34:32.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out of my way, you. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.36,0:34:35.11,Default,,0,0,0,,(ELEPHANT TRUMPETS)
Dialogue: 0,0:34:36.82,0:34:38.57,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: A drug person\Ncan learn to cope\Nwith things like
Dialogue: 0,0:34:38.66,0:34:41.74,Default,,0,0,0,,seeing their dead grandmother\Ncrawling up their leg\Nwith a knife in her teeth,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.83,0:34:44.50,Default,,0,0,0,,but nobody should be asked\Nto handle this trip.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:45.33,0:34:48.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Bazooko Circus\Nis what the whole hep world\Nwould be doing Saturday night
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.59,0:34:50.59,Default,,0,0,0,,if the Nazis had won the War.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.67,0:34:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,This was the Sixth Reich.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:52.30,0:34:55.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Place your bets!\NWhere everyone's a winner\Nand nobody's a loser!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.51,0:34:59.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Step right up and shoot\Nthe pasties off the nipples\Nof a 1 0-foot bull dyke
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.97,0:35:01.89,Default,,0,0,0,,and win a cotton candy goat!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.02,0:35:05.89,Default,,0,0,0,,(JABBERING)
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.90,0:35:07.94,Default,,0,0,0,,(BLOWS RASPBERRY)
Dialogue: 0,0:35:08.02,0:35:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Step up to this\Nfantastic machine!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:09.86,0:35:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,For just 99 cents,\Nyour likeness will\Nappear 200 feet tall
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.86,0:35:15.82,Default,,0,0,0,,on a screen over\Ndowntown Las Vegas.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:15.91,0:35:18.36,Default,,0,0,0,,For just 99 cents more\Nyou can have a voice message!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:18.45,0:35:19.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Say whatever you want,\Nfellow!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.91,0:35:21.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, they'll hear you,\Nall right!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.37,0:35:23.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll be 200 feet tall !
Dialogue: 0,0:35:24.58,0:35:26.46,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: The ether\Nwas wearing off.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.54,0:35:28.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The acid was long gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:29.17,0:35:31.13,Default,,0,0,0,,But the mescaline\Nwas running strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:31.21,0:35:32.25,Default,,0,0,0,,(MAN CHATTERING)
Dialogue: 0,0:35:32.34,0:35:34.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Good mescaline comes on slow.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:34.80,0:35:36.97,Default,,0,0,0,,The first hour's all waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.05,0:35:39.22,Default,,0,0,0,,And then about\Nhalfway through\Nits second hour,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:39.30,0:35:42.47,Default,,0,0,0,,you start cursing\Nthe creep who burned you\Nbecause nothing's happening.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:42.56,0:35:44.56,Default,,0,0,0,,And then, zang!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.10,0:35:48.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate to say this\Nbut this place\Nis getting to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.94,0:35:52.44,Default,,0,0,0,,(HICCUPPING)\NI think I'm getting the fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.53,0:35:54.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.15,0:35:55.65,Default,,0,0,0,,We came here to find\Nthe American Dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:55.74,0:35:58.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that we're\Nright in the vortex,\Nyou wanna quit?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:58.74,0:36:01.28,Default,,0,0,0,,You must realize, man,\Nwe've found the main nerve.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.37,0:36:03.74,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what\Ngives me the fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.83,0:36:05.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, look!\NWhat?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.54,0:36:09.46,Default,,0,0,0,,There's two women\Nfucking a polar bear.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.54,0:36:11.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me\Nthose things.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:12.04,0:36:13.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Not now, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:14.96,0:36:16.76,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my last drink.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:16.88,0:36:18.68,Default,,0,0,0,,How much money\Ncan you lend me?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:18.76,0:36:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Not much. Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.43,0:36:22.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to go.\NGo?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:22.43,0:36:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Leave the country.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:24.56,0:36:26.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no. Calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.10,0:36:27.60,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll be straight\Nin a few hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.68,0:36:29.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Just sit down.\NSit the fuck down.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.23,0:36:32.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't fuck around, man.\NThis is serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.19,0:36:35.11,Default,,0,0,0,,One more hour in this town,\NI'll kill somebody.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.57,0:36:38.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay,\NI'll lend you some money.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.03,0:36:41.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Come with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:41.91,0:36:43.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanna leave fast.\NOkay.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.62,0:36:46.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's pay this bill,\Nget up very slowly.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:47.70,0:36:49.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it's gonna\Nbe a long walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.75,0:36:51.12,Default,,0,0,0,,WOMAN: Light, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.42,0:36:56.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Do they pay you\Nto screw that bear?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:56.51,0:36:59.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.30,0:37:01.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What the fuck\Ndid he say to me?\NHe's drunk.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:01.55,0:37:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd better take care\Nof your friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.72,0:37:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam, sir, baby, child,\Nwhatever, can I pay?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:06.47,0:37:08.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, take this.\NThat should be enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:08.60,0:37:11.31,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, come on.\NLet's go downstairs\Nand gamble.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:14.32,0:37:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You guys don't\Nfucking give up.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:16.82,0:37:18.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Where'd he go?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.86,0:37:20.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did he go?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:24.32,0:37:26.49,Default,,0,0,0,,When is this\Nthing gonna stop?\NStop?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:26.62,0:37:29.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop it!\NIt won't stop.\NIt's never gonna stop, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:30.04,0:37:31.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't move. You'll fall down.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:32.33,0:37:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck, he's. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:37:34.84,0:37:37.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did he go? Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.55,0:37:39.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on. Let go.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:39.84,0:37:42.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Quick, like a bunny.\NHop! Hop!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.80,0:37:44.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on. Hop!\NI can't!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:44.64,0:37:48.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you sniveling,\Nchicken shit bastard !\NStop it!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.48,0:37:53.06,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:59.78,0:38:00.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.45,0:38:03.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NYou fell, you fell. Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:03.36,0:38:05.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Son of a bitch.\NYou pushed me.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:05.91,0:38:07.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Go away!\NCome on.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:07.87,0:38:10.29,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. You stay here\Nand go to jail. I'm leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:11.16,0:38:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, you fiend !
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.83,0:38:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Step right over. . .\NNothing. I want nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.79,0:38:16.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you see that?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:17.42,0:38:18.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.55,0:38:20.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Some son of a bitch\Njust kicked me in the back.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.01,0:38:22.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Probably the bartender.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.13,0:38:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Wanted to stomp you\Nfor what you said\Nto the waitress.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:24.26,0:38:27.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Holy moley! Holy moley!\NCows are gonna kill me!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.22,0:38:29.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Bisexuals are gonna kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:29.81,0:38:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's get out of here.\NWhere's the elevator?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.52,0:38:33.31,Default,,0,0,0,,No, fuck! Don't go\Nnear the elevator, man !
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.39,0:38:35.14,Default,,0,0,0,,That's just what\Nthey want us to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:35.23,0:38:39.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Trap us in a steel box,\Ntake us down to the basement.\NCome here.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:40.03,0:38:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,(GUN FIRING)
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.61,0:38:43.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't run, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:43.70,0:38:45.78,Default,,0,0,0,,They'd like any excuse\Nto shoot us.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:48.53,0:38:50.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You drive. You drive.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.54,0:38:54.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I think there's\Nsomething wrong with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:00.46,0:39:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Wrong door. Wrong door.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:03.01,0:39:05.51,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NThis is not a good town\Nfor psychedelic drugs.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:06.43,0:39:08.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Extremely menacing vibrations\Nwere all around us.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:09.89,0:39:11.43,Default,,0,0,0,,We finally made it\Nto the room,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.02,0:39:14.02,Default,,0,0,0,,but the key\Nwouldn't open the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:15.23,0:39:17.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Those bastards have changed\Nthe lock on us, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:18.44,0:39:19.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Already?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:20.36,0:39:22.98,Default,,0,0,0,,They probably\Nsearched the room, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:23.61,0:39:25.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Jesus Christ,\Nwe're finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:28.66,0:39:30.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Move out of the way.\NLook out! Look out!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:31.20,0:39:32.62,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTS)
Dialogue: 0,0:39:33.16,0:39:34.16,Default,,0,0,0,,(EXCLAIMS)
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.29,0:39:36.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Bolt everything !\NUse all the chains!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:36.92,0:39:37.92,Default,,0,0,0,,(MUMBLING)
Dialogue: 0,0:39:39.34,0:39:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That's better. That's better.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.51,0:39:45.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did this one come from?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:47.80,0:39:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,That's Lacerda's.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:49.30,0:39:51.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Yeah.\NI thought we might need it.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:52.43,0:39:55.14,Default,,0,0,0,,What for?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:55.23,0:39:58.85,Default,,0,0,0,,So we can go up there\Nand blast him out of bed
Dialogue: 0,0:39:58.94,0:40:00.36,Default,,0,0,0,,with a fire hose, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:01.32,0:40:03.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I think we should leave\Nthat poor bastard alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:03.78,0:40:05.53,Default,,0,0,0,,He told me he was\Ngonna turn in early, so. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:40:05.61,0:40:07.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.66,0:40:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,He got a hold\Nof my woman, man !
Dialogue: 0,0:40:10.87,0:40:13.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean that blonde groupie\Nwith the film crew?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:14.37,0:40:16.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit.\NThink he sodomized her?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:16.58,0:40:18.41,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.\NLaugh about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:18.50,0:40:19.83,Default,,0,0,0,,He's gluing her eyes\Nshut right now, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:19.92,0:40:25.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You goddamn honkies\Nare all the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:27.01,0:40:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Jesus God Almighty, man,\Nwhere'd you get\Nthat big fucker?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:31.18,0:40:33.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Room service sent it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:33.35,0:40:36.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I needed something\Nto cut the limes, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:37.18,0:40:39.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Limes? What limes?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:39.98,0:40:41.10,Default,,0,0,0,,They didn't have any.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:41.19,0:40:43.11,Default,,0,0,0,,They don't grow\Nin the desert.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:43.19,0:40:45.36,Default,,0,0,0,,That dirty toad bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:46.36,0:40:49.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Should've taken him out\Nwhen I had a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:49.86,0:40:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,(ROARS)
Dialogue: 0,0:40:51.41,0:40:53.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Now he has her, man !
Dialogue: 0,0:40:54.53,0:40:56.83,Default,,0,0,0,,He got a hold of my baby,\Nyeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:57.33,0:40:59.20,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\Nl remembered the girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:59.66,0:41:02.62,Default,,0,0,0,,We'd had a problem with her\Nin the elevator\Na few hours earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:02.71,0:41:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,My attorney had\Nmade a fool of himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:06.05,0:41:07.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you look\Njust like him.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:07.97,0:41:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,You think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:16.93,0:41:18.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You must be a rider.\NHmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.23,0:41:23.27,Default,,0,0,0,,She's speaking to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:27.86,0:41:29.74,Default,,0,0,0,,What class are you in?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:29.82,0:41:31.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Class?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:31.24,0:41:33.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What the fuck do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:33.32,0:41:35.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you ride?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:35.37,0:41:39.16,Default,,0,0,0,,See, we're here getting\Na little footage\Non the race for
Dialogue: 0,0:41:39.45,0:41:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,a television series.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:41.50,0:41:43.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought maybe\Nwe could use you.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:45.25,0:41:47.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, use me? I ride a. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:41:48.17,0:41:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,"Mother of God," l thought.\NHere it comes.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:51.34,0:41:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I ride the big fuckers.\NYou know? Big ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:54.68,0:41:56.93,Default,,0,0,0,,The really big fuckers. Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:57.35,0:41:59.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Vincent Black Shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.14,0:42:01.06,Default,,0,0,0,,We're with the factory team.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.14,0:42:02.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.\NBullshit.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.52,0:42:03.60,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:03.69,0:42:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Bullshit.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:05.48,0:42:06.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:08.15,0:42:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I think there's\Nsome kind of ignorant,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.78,0:42:11.28,Default,,0,0,0,,chicken shit. . .\NMove over, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:11.36,0:42:14.24,Default,,0,0,0,,An ignorant chicken\Nfucker in this town.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:15.57,0:42:17.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You pink motherfucker.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:17.91,0:42:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I can show you\Nbetter than I can\Ntell you, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:20.70,0:42:22.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Got a light?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:24.71,0:42:26.00,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:31.47,0:42:33.84,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't trust me, do you?\NHuh?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:35.26,0:42:37.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Put the smile away.\NIt's okay.\NI know these guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:37.47,0:42:39.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep trying me, jerk-off.\NKeep trying me.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:40.06,0:42:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,You wanna impress her?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:41.35,0:42:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, impress her with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:44.27,0:42:45.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, fuck.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:45.65,0:42:46.98,Default,,0,0,0,,(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)
Dialogue: 0,0:42:52.99,0:42:54.15,Default,,0,0,0,,(GONZO WHOOPS)
Dialogue: 0,0:42:54.24,0:42:56.95,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you goddamn freak! Freak!
Dialogue: 0,0:42:59.03,0:43:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,The police will be\Ncoming after you.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:01.87,0:43:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) For your Iove
Dialogue: 0,0:43:02.100,0:43:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me the key.\NGive me the goddamn key!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:07.17,0:43:08.59,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) For your Iove
Dialogue: 0,0:43:08.67,0:43:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,(WHOOPS)
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.26,0:43:13.34,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) For your Iove
Dialogue: 0,0:43:13.42,0:43:15.97,Default,,0,0,0,,l give you everything and more
Dialogue: 0,0:43:16.05,0:43:17.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Put the knife away.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.39,0:43:18.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I been walking all day.\NCome on.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:18.68,0:43:20.80,Default,,0,0,0,,It's in my pocket. Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:22.10,0:43:23.27,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) For your Iove
Dialogue: 0,0:43:23.35,0:43:27.81,Default,,0,0,0,,l give you everything\Nl give you diamonds
Dialogue: 0,0:43:27.90,0:43:30.02,Default,,0,0,0,,l know the place\Nthat will excite
Dialogue: 0,0:43:31.07,0:43:32.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn it.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:33.24,0:43:35.36,Default,,0,0,0,,It's serious now, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:37.53,0:43:39.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That girl understood, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.91,0:43:42.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Whew.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:43.04,0:43:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,She fell in love with me, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.41,0:43:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Eye contact, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:49.00,0:43:50.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:55.05,0:43:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,(GROANS)
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.01,0:43:58.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I should go up there\Nand castrate that fucker.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:59.01,0:44:01.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take the blame, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:01.76,0:44:04.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's just leave that\Nweird fucker alone, man.\NCome on.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:05.10,0:44:07.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you made\Na deal with him?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:07.94,0:44:11.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you put him on to her?\NHuh? Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:13.15,0:44:14.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:15.61,0:44:17.15,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, look. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:44:18.07,0:44:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,You better put\Nthat goddamn blade away, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:20.78,0:44:22.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Get your fucking head\Nstraight.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:23.03,0:44:24.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna go get\Nthe car washed.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:25.45,0:44:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NOne of the things you learn
Dialogue: 0,0:44:26.79,0:44:28.91,Default,,0,0,0,,after years of dealing\Nwith drug people,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:28.100,0:44:31.29,Default,,0,0,0,,is that you can turn\Nyour back on a person,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:31.38,0:44:34.30,Default,,0,0,0,,but never turn\Nyour back on a drug.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:34.51,0:44:37.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Especially when it's waving\Na razor-sharp hunting knife\Nin your eye.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:38.43,0:44:39.43,Default,,0,0,0,,(BELL DINGS)
Dialogue: 0,0:44:40.51,0:44:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,(WOMAN SOBBING)
Dialogue: 0,0:44:44.14,0:44:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,(SLOT MACHINE CLICKING)
Dialogue: 0,0:44:46.10,0:44:48.52,Default,,0,0,0,,What was l doing out here?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:48.60,0:44:50.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What was the meaning\Nof this trip?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:51.65,0:44:54.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Was l just roaming around\Nin a drug frenzy of some kind?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:55.23,0:44:58.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Or had l really come\Nout here to Las Vegas\Nto work on a story?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:04.78,0:45:07.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are these people,\Nthese faces?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:08.83,0:45:10.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Where do they come from?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:11.58,0:45:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,They look like caricatures\Nof used car dealers\Nfrom Dallas.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:14.80,0:45:16.30,Default,,0,0,0,,And, sweet Jesus,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.38,0:45:18.80,Default,,0,0,0,,there are a hell\Nof a lot of them\Nat 4:30 on a Sunday morning,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:20.09,0:45:21.80,Default,,0,0,0,,still humping\Nthe American Dream,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:22.80,0:45:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,that vision of the big winner\Nsomehow emerging
Dialogue: 0,0:45:24.89,0:45:28.77,Default,,0,0,0,,from the last-minute,\Npre-dawn chaos\Nof a stale Vegas casino.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:29.10,0:45:31.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Twenty.\NWe change a 20.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:31.89,0:45:33.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:34.31,0:45:36.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we go.\NOkay.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:36.11,0:45:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Spinning the wheeI,\Nspinning the wheel,\Nspinning the wheel
Dialogue: 0,0:45:38.94,0:45:41.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Make me rich\NMake me very rich
Dialogue: 0,0:45:41.74,0:45:42.86,Default,,0,0,0,,(EXCLAIMING)
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.95,0:45:43.99,Default,,0,0,0,,That's 1 0.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:44.07,0:45:45.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you bastard !
Dialogue: 0,0:45:46.70,0:45:47.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit.\NSorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.87,0:45:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: No, no.\NCalm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:50.91,0:45:52.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Learn to enjoy losing.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:57.46,0:45:59.55,Default,,0,0,0,,(HEAVY METAL MUSIC PLAYING)
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.77,0:46:15.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck, man, it's the fucking\NGreat Deluge in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:15.19,0:46:16.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't touch that.\NLeave it alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:16.65,0:46:18.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't fuck with it, man !
Dialogue: 0,0:46:18.98,0:46:20.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Jesus Christ.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:22.61,0:46:24.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:25.53,0:46:27.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you eat all this acid?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:27.20,0:46:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right. Music!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.54,0:46:31.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You better pray to God\Nthere's some Thorazine\Nin that bag.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:31.66,0:46:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, you're in\Nbad fucking trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:33.12,0:46:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Music, man,\Nput that tape on !
Dialogue: 0,0:46:35.63,0:46:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What tape?\NJefferson Airplane.\NWhite Rabbit.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:38.21,0:46:39.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I need a rising sound.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.84,0:46:41.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You're doomed.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:41.13,0:46:42.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm leaving here\Nin two hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:42.47,0:46:44.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Then they're gonna come up\Nhere and beat the mortal shit\Nout of you
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.01,0:46:46.76,Default,,0,0,0,,right there\Nin that fucking tub.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:47.14,0:46:48.47,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTING)
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.55,0:46:49.97,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, I'll do it!\NI'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.06,0:46:51.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll do it. Fuck, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:51.93,0:46:54.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Just do me one last favor,\Nwill you?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:54.64,0:46:56.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me two hours.\NThat's all I ask, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:57.15,0:46:59.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Two hours to sleep\Nbefore tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:00.19,0:47:01.94,Default,,0,0,0,,This is fixed.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:02.03,0:47:03.74,Default,,0,0,0,,It's gonna be\Na very difficult day.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:04.86,0:47:06.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll give you all\Nthe time you need.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:06.74,0:47:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Electrocution.\NWe don't want that.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:10.24,0:47:11.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck off.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:11.29,0:47:12.29,Default,,0,0,0,,(FARTS)
Dialogue: 0,0:47:14.41,0:47:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) When Iogic\Nand proportion have fallen
Dialogue: 0,0:47:19.50,0:47:21.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:21.17,0:47:23.17,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) SIoppy dead
Dialogue: 0,0:47:23.26,0:47:26.51,Default,,0,0,0,,And the White Knight\Nis talking backwards
Dialogue: 0,0:47:26.59,0:47:27.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:27.80,0:47:31.97,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) And the Red Queen's\Noff with her head
Dialogue: 0,0:47:32.39,0:47:33.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember
Dialogue: 0,0:47:33.60,0:47:37.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God Almighty.\NGONZO: Help! Help!\NHelp me! Help!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:37.94,0:47:39.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit! He's killing himself!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:39.40,0:47:41.52,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING)\NWhat the dormouse said
Dialogue: 0,0:47:41.61,0:47:42.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't touch it, man.\NDon't touch it!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:42.99,0:47:44.53,Default,,0,0,0,,(GROANING)
Dialogue: 0,0:47:44.78,0:47:46.07,Default,,0,0,0,,For fuck's sake, man !
Dialogue: 0,0:47:46.15,0:47:47.74,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Feed your head
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.82,0:47:48.82,Default,,0,0,0,,(MUTTERING)
Dialogue: 0,0:47:51.33,0:47:53.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Back, God. . .\NBack, motherfucker!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:53.62,0:47:55.95,Default,,0,0,0,,(GASPING)
Dialogue: 0,0:47:56.71,0:47:58.88,Default,,0,0,0,,On a roll, man !\NI need it again !
Dialogue: 0,0:47:58.96,0:48:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.38,0:48:02.71,Default,,0,0,0,,When it comes to\Nthat fantastic note,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:02.80,0:48:03.88,Default,,0,0,0,,(PANTING)
Dialogue: 0,0:48:03.96,0:48:07.26,Default,,0,0,0,,when the rabbit\Nbites its own head off.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:08.26,0:48:12.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to throw\Nthat fucking radio
Dialogue: 0,0:48:13.26,0:48:16.06,Default,,0,0,0,,into the tub with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:16.14,0:48:18.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck, you've gone\Ncompletely sideways, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:18.56,0:48:19.94,Default,,0,0,0,,That'll blast you\Nright through the wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:20.02,0:48:21.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll be stone dead\Nin 1 0 seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:21.82,0:48:23.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck, they'll make me\Nexplain things. Shit.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:23.40,0:48:24.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Bullshit.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:27.03,0:48:30.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't fuck with me now, man.\NI am Ahab.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:34.20,0:48:35.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Jesus Christ.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:36.79,0:48:39.41,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, you weird fucker!\NSit down ! Back in the tub!
Dialogue: 0,0:48:39.50,0:48:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll plunge this into\Nyour fucking throat.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:43.17,0:48:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't make me use this,\Nman.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:47.38,0:48:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:49.51,0:48:51.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Probably the only solution.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:51.89,0:48:54.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me make sure\NI've got this all lined up.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:55.26,0:48:57.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You want me to
Dialogue: 0,0:48:57.22,0:49:00.39,Default,,0,0,0,,throw this thing into the tub\Nwhen White Rabbit peaks,\Nis that it?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:00.48,0:49:01.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, fuck.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:04.02,0:49:07.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I was beginning to think\NI was gonna have to go outside
Dialogue: 0,0:49:07.44,0:49:09.78,Default,,0,0,0,,and get one of the\Ngoddamn maids to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:09.86,0:49:12.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no. I'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:12.62,0:49:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit. What are friends for?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:16.62,0:49:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,(GROANING)
Dialogue: 0,0:49:17.87,0:49:20.41,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) I think she'II know
Dialogue: 0,0:49:20.67,0:49:21.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:22.88,0:49:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Where Iogic
Dialogue: 0,0:49:24.54,0:49:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Close your eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:25.67,0:49:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) And proportion
Dialogue: 0,0:49:26.84,0:49:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, good boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.92,0:49:30.59,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING)\NHave fallen sloppy dead
Dialogue: 0,0:49:31.22,0:49:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Rabbit! White Rabbit!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:33.09,0:49:35.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Quiet, goddamn it!\NYou're wasting my time!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.68,0:49:39.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Higher, man. Higher.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.35,0:49:40.85,Default,,0,0,0,,(VOLUME INCREASES)
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.94,0:49:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Remember
Dialogue: 0,0:49:42.06,0:49:45.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, close those peepers.\NTen.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.65,0:49:48.07,Default,,0,0,0,,(GROANING)\NWhat the dormouse said
Dialogue: 0,0:49:48.44,0:49:50.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Nine. 1 1 1 !
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.07,0:49:52.11,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Feed your head
Dialogue: 0,0:49:52.20,0:49:53.45,Default,,0,0,0,,52!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:54.57,0:49:55.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Feed your head
Dialogue: 0,0:49:55.70,0:49:57.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Hey! Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:11.22,0:50:12.84,Default,,0,0,0,,(GONZO SHRIEKING)
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.40,0:50:28.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You bastard !
Dialogue: 0,0:50:29.57,0:50:32.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Mace! Mace, man.\NYou want this?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.36,0:50:36.74,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd do that,\Nwouldn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:36.82,0:50:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:37.95,0:50:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You fucking bastard !
Dialogue: 0,0:50:39.45,0:50:42.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell, just a minute ago\Nyou were asking me\Nto kill you.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:42.71,0:50:44.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Now you wanna kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.54,0:50:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What l should do, goddamn it,\Nis call the fucking police!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:47.38,0:50:49.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, are you upset.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:51.21,0:50:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,There'd be no point, man,\Ncalling the cops.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:54.59,0:50:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:56.64,0:50:59.80,Default,,0,0,0,,l wouldn't dare go to sleep\Nwith you wandering around\Nwith a head full of acid
Dialogue: 0,0:50:59.89,0:51:02.27,Default,,0,0,0,,wanting to slice me up\Nwith that goddamn knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:03.31,0:51:05.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Who said anything\Nabout slicing you up, man?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:08.32,0:51:11.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I just wanted to cut\Na little "Z" in your forehead.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:11.53,0:51:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,(WHEEZING LAUGHTER)
Dialogue: 0,0:51:13.45,0:51:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Get back in the tub.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:15.36,0:51:17.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Eat some reds\Nand try to calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:18.03,0:51:20.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Smoke some grass.\NShoot some fucking smack.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:20.70,0:51:23.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit, man, do whatever\Nyou gotta do, but please,
Dialogue: 0,0:51:24.33,0:51:27.46,Default,,0,0,0,,l need some fucking rest, man.\NPlease. Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:27.96,0:51:29.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Get up, you pig fucker!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:30.96,0:51:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Up! Up!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:33.67,0:51:35.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I, uh. . .
Dialogue: 0,0:51:36.89,0:51:38.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:39.80,0:51:41.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You need to get to work.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:42.47,0:51:44.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn, what a bummer.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:45.02,0:51:46.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You scurvy shyster bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:47.31,0:51:49.48,Default,,0,0,0,,l'm a Doctor of Journalism,\Nman.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:49.56,0:51:50.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:51.82,0:51:53.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't let me keep you up.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:53.19,0:51:55.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Now...\NDon't let me keep you up.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.03,0:51:59.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Get in there\Nand clean your shorts!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:59.16,0:52:02.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Clean your shorts, goddamn it,\Nlike a big boy. Go on!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:03.16,0:52:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Pig!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:08.42,0:52:10.21,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: The acid\Nhad shifted gears on him.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:10.88,0:52:12.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The next phase\Nwould probably be
Dialogue: 0,0:52:12.21,0:52:14.46,Default,,0,0,0,,one of those\Nhellishly intense\Nintrospective nightmares.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.55,0:52:16.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Must get some peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:16.17,0:52:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NFour hours or so\Nof catatonic despair.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:20.22,0:52:21.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn drugs.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:23.39,0:52:24.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:29.56,0:52:31.98,Default,,0,0,0,,lgnore the nightmare\Nin the bathroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:33.23,0:52:35.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Just another ugly refugee\Nfrom the love generation.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:37.74,0:52:40.07,Default,,0,0,0,,My attorney had\Nnever been able\Nto accept the notion
Dialogue: 0,0:52:40.16,0:52:42.57,Default,,0,0,0,,often espoused by\Nformer drug abusers
Dialogue: 0,0:52:42.83,0:52:45.12,Default,,0,0,0,,that you can get a lot higher\Nwithout drugs than with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:46.58,0:52:48.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And neither have l,\Nfor that matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:48.66,0:52:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING)\NWhen the truth is found
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.46,0:52:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,To be lies
Dialogue: 0,0:52:55.92,0:52:58.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And all the joy
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.63,0:53:02.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Within you dies
Dialogue: 0,0:53:02.55,0:53:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you want\Nsomebody to love
Dialogue: 0,0:53:06.06,0:53:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you need\Nsomebody to love
Dialogue: 0,0:53:09.77,0:53:13.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Wouldn't you love\Nsomebody to love
Dialogue: 0,0:53:13.44,0:53:18.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You better find\Nsomebody to love
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.49,0:53:20.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Love
Dialogue: 0,0:53:22.53,0:53:26.45,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: 1965.\NThe great San Francisco\Nacid wave.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:26.74,0:53:29.08,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING)\NWhen the garden flowers
Dialogue: 0,0:53:29.37,0:53:31.92,Default,,0,0,0,,l recall one night\Nin a place called the Matrix.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:32.46,0:53:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,There l was.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:34.17,0:53:36.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother of God. There l am.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:37.84,0:53:39.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Holy fuck.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.88,0:53:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Clearly l was a victim\Nof the drug explosion,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:43.97,0:53:47.31,Default,,0,0,0,,a natural street freak just\Neating whatever came by.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:47.51,0:53:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Does anybody want some LSD?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:53.40,0:53:58.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I got all the makings\Nright here!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:59.15,0:54:04.16,Default,,0,0,0,,(ECHOING)\NAll I need is a place\Nto cook.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:08.37,0:54:11.12,Default,,0,0,0,,l decided to eat only\Nhalf of the acid at first.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:11.21,0:54:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,But l spilled the rest\Non the sleeve of\Nmy red woolen shirt.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:20.51,0:54:23.72,Default,,0,0,0,,(ECHOING)\NWhat's the trouble?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:24.93,0:54:29.89,Default,,0,0,0,,(ECHOING) Well, all this\Nwhite stuff on my sleeve
Dialogue: 0,0:54:32.27,0:54:35.31,Default,,0,0,0,,is LSD.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:51.29,0:54:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE: With a bit of luck,\Nhis life was ruined forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:56.04,0:55:00.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Always thinking that just\Nbehind some narrow door\Nin all his favorite bars,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:00.42,0:55:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,men in red woolen shirts\Nare getting incredible kicks\Nfrom things he'll never know.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:12.60,0:55:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Strange memories\Non this nervous night\Nin Las Vegas.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:16.31,0:55:19.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Has it been five years? Six?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:20.98,0:55:26.20,Default,,0,0,0,,lt seems like a lifetime,\Nthe kind of peak\Nthat never comes again.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:26.28,0:55:28.66,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Love is but a song\Nwe're singing
Dialogue: 0,0:55:29.16,0:55:31.49,Default,,0,0,0,,San Francisco\Nin the middle '60s
Dialogue: 0,0:55:31.70,0:55:34.37,Default,,0,0,0,,was a very special time\Nand place to be a part of,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:35.83,0:55:36.96,Default,,0,0,0,,but no explanation.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:37.04,0:55:38.29,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) We can make\Nthe mountains ring
Dialogue: 0,0:55:38.38,0:55:40.38,Default,,0,0,0,,No mix of words\Nor music or memories
Dialogue: 0,0:55:40.46,0:55:43.55,Default,,0,0,0,,can touch\Nthat sense of knowing\Nthat you were there and alive
Dialogue: 0,0:55:44.01,0:55:47.72,Default,,0,0,0,,in that corner of time\Nin the world,\Nwhatever it meant.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:48.22,0:55:51.14,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING)\NThough the bird is on the wing
Dialogue: 0,0:55:51.81,0:55:55.18,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING)\NAnd you may not know why
Dialogue: 0,0:55:57.85,0:56:00.90,Default,,0,0,0,,There was madness\Nin any direction,\Nat any hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:00.98,0:56:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Come on peopIe, now
Dialogue: 0,0:56:02.44,0:56:03.90,Default,,0,0,0,,You could strike sparks\Nanywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:03.99,0:56:05.53,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING)\NTry to love one another
Dialogue: 0,0:56:05.61,0:56:07.32,Default,,0,0,0,,There was a fantastic\Nuniversal sense
Dialogue: 0,0:56:07.41,0:56:09.66,Default,,0,0,0,,that whatever we were doing\Nwas right,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:09.74,0:56:11.28,Default,,0,0,0,,that we were winning.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:12.41,0:56:14.24,Default,,0,0,0,,And that, l think,\Nwas the handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:14.33,0:56:16.29,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Some may come\Nand some may go
Dialogue: 0,0:56:16.37,0:56:19.62,Default,,0,0,0,,That sense of inevitable\Nvictory over the forces\Nof old and evil.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.50,0:56:23.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Not in any mean\Nor military sense,\Nwe didn't need that.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:25.42,0:56:27.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Our energy would\Nsimply prevail.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:28.68,0:56:30.43,Default,,0,0,0,,We had all the momentum.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.18,0:56:34.68,Default,,0,0,0,,We were riding the crest\Nof a high and beautiful wave.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:36.93,0:56:40.35,Default,,0,0,0,,So now,\Nless than 5 years later,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:41.48,0:56:44.48,Default,,0,0,0,,you can go up a steep hill\Nin Las Vegas and look west
Dialogue: 0,0:56:44.98,0:56:47.11,Default,,0,0,0,,and with the right kind\Nof eyes,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:47.86,0:56:50.03,Default,,0,0,0,,you can almost see\Nthe high-water mark,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:50.99,0:56:55.33,Default,,0,0,0,,that place where\Nthe wave finally broke\Nand rolled back.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:55.41,0:56:57.41,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Try to Iove\None another right now
Dialogue: 0,0:57:02.29,0:57:04.25,Default,,0,0,0,,(ELECTRIC PIANO PLAYING)
Dialogue: 0,0:57:10.34,0:57:11.39,Default,,0,0,0,,(DOORBELL BUZZING)
Dialogue: 0,0:57:11.84,0:57:14.26,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Want some whiskey\Nin your water?\NRoom service!
Dialogue: 0,0:57:14.35,0:57:16.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Some sugar in your tea?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:16.10,0:57:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What's all these crazy\Nquestions they're asking me?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:19.31,0:57:20.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:20.44,0:57:21.77,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the craziest party\Nthere could ever be
Dialogue: 0,0:57:21.86,0:57:24.86,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you want, man?\NWhat do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:24.94,0:57:26.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Room service.\NGet out.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:26.90,0:57:27.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama told me not to come
Dialogue: 0,0:57:28.03,0:57:30.24,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not mine.\NYou're in the wrong room.\NGet out! Get the fuck out!
Dialogue: 0,0:57:30.32,0:57:32.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I've got a gun.\NIt's not mine, really.\NGet out.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:32.78,0:57:33.95,Default,,0,0,0,,The. . . The. . . The. . .\NWhat?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:34.03,0:57:35.24,Default,,0,0,0,,The bill.\NAll right.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:35.33,0:57:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you sign for it?\NYeah, I'll get it. Hurry up.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.100,0:57:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't move, man.\NBe very still. There we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:43.25,0:57:44.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Say nothing to no one, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:44.71,0:57:47.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Open up the window\NLet some air into this room
Dialogue: 0,0:57:47.96,0:57:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NThe decision to flee\Ncame suddenly.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:51.38,0:57:52.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Or maybe not.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:52.51,0:57:54.64,Default,,0,0,0,,That cigarette you're smoking\Nabout scared me half to death
Dialogue: 0,0:57:54.72,0:57:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe l'd planned it\Nall along, subconsciously\Nwaiting for the right moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:59.06,0:58:00.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama told me not to come
Dialogue: 0,0:58:00.18,0:58:01.98,Default,,0,0,0,,The bill was a factor,\Nl think,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:02.06,0:58:03.31,Default,,0,0,0,,because l had no money\Nto pay for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:03.40,0:58:04.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama told me not to come
Dialogue: 0,0:58:04.90,0:58:06.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Our room service tabs\Nhad been running
Dialogue: 0,0:58:06.40,0:58:09.40,Default,,0,0,0,,somewhere between\N29 and 36 dollars per hour
Dialogue: 0,0:58:09.49,0:58:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,for 48 consecutive hours.\Nlncredible.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:12.74,0:58:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,That ain't the way\Nto have fun, son
Dialogue: 0,0:58:13.86,0:58:15.82,Default,,0,0,0,,How could it happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:15.91,0:58:18.16,Default,,0,0,0,,But by the time\Nl asked this question,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:18.24,0:58:20.50,Default,,0,0,0,,there was no one around\Nto answer it.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:20.58,0:58:23.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That rotten attorney of mine,\NDr. Gonzo, was gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:23.92,0:58:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,He must have sensed trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:26.63,0:58:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm? Oh. A "Z"?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:30.22,0:58:31.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Panic.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:32.72,0:58:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,lt crept up my spine\Nlike first-rising vibes\Nof an acid frenzy.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:37.30,0:58:39.89,Default,,0,0,0,,All these horrible realities\Nbegan to dawn on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:39.97,0:58:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE: Oh, fuck.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:43.81,0:58:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: Here I was,\Nalone in Las Vegas,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:47.23,0:58:48.86,Default,,0,0,0,,completely twisted on drugs.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:48.94,0:58:51.99,Default,,0,0,0,,No cash,\Nno story for the magazine,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:52.15,0:58:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,and on top of everything else\Nl had a gigantic goddamn\Nhotel bill to deal with.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:59.58,0:59:03.04,Default,,0,0,0,,l didn't even know\Nwho'd won the race.\NMaybe nobody.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:04.21,0:59:06.42,Default,,0,0,0,,How would Horatio Alger\Nhave handled this situation?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:08.17,0:59:10.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Stay calm. Stay calm.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:11.67,0:59:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,l'm a relatively\Nrespectable citizen.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:14.13,0:59:17.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Multiple felon, perhaps,\Nbut certainly not dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:18.05,0:59:19.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Taxi !
Dialogue: 0,0:59:19.72,0:59:21.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Luckily, l had taken\Nthe soap and grapefruit
Dialogue: 0,0:59:21.81,0:59:24.56,Default,,0,0,0,,and other luggage\Nout to the car\Na few hours earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:24.64,0:59:27.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, it was only a matter\Nof slipping the noose.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:27.98,0:59:29.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Here, take this.\NAll right.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:32.69,0:59:34.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Duke! Mr. Duke!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:34.57,0:59:36.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, shit.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:37.20,0:59:38.49,Default,,0,0,0,,We've been looking for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:38.57,0:59:40.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The game was up.\NThey had me.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:41.58,0:59:43.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Many fine books have been\Nwritten in prison, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:44.100,0:59:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir?\NWhat?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:47.83,0:59:49.21,Default,,0,0,0,,This telegram came for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:49.29,0:59:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, it's not for you.\NIt's for somebody named\NThompson.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:52.34,0:59:53.80,Default,,0,0,0,,But it says,\N"Care of Raoul Duke."
Dialogue: 0,0:59:53.88,0:59:56.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you. . . Do you. . .\NDoes that mean anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:56.38,0:59:57.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, yes, it means a lot.\NThanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:59.01,1:00:01.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I checked the register\Nfor this man Thompson.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:01.35,1:00:03.47,Default,,0,0,0,,We don't show him,\Nbut I figured he might\Nbe part of your team.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:03.56,1:00:05.10,Default,,0,0,0,,He is. Don't worry.\NI'll get it to him.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:05.18,1:00:07.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. What confused us was
Dialogue: 0,1:00:07.89,1:00:10.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. Gonzo's signature\Non the telegram\Nfrom Los Angeles
Dialogue: 0,1:00:10.69,1:00:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,when we knew he was\Nright here in the hotel.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:13.28,1:00:15.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.\NYou did the right thing.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:15.70,1:00:17.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Never try to understand\Na press message.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:17.70,1:00:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,About half the time,\Nwe use codes.\NEspecially with Dr. Gonzo.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:20.70,1:00:21.95,Default,,0,0,0,,See you.\NTell me. . .
Dialogue: 0,1:00:22.03,1:00:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,(TIRES SCREECHING)
Dialogue: 0,1:00:26.37,1:00:28.12,Default,,0,0,0,,When will the doctor\Nbe awake?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:28.21,1:00:29.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Awake? What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:29.96,1:00:34.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, my manager, Mr. Heem,\Nwould like to meet him.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:35.88,1:00:40.22,Default,,0,0,0,,It's nothing unusual,\NMr. Heem likes to meet\Nall of our large accounts,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:42.14,1:00:43.72,Default,,0,0,0,,put them on a personal basis,\Nyou know?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:43.81,1:00:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Just a chat and a handshake.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:45.68,1:00:47.06,Default,,0,0,0,,You understand.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:47.18,1:00:49.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, but if I were you,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:49.35,1:00:51.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I would leave the\Ndoctor alone until after\Nhe's eaten his breakfast
Dialogue: 0,1:00:51.36,1:00:53.23,Default,,0,0,0,,because he's\Na very crude man.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:53.82,1:00:55.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Jesus God !
Dialogue: 0,1:00:56.03,1:00:57.19,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,1:00:58.95,1:01:02.49,Default,,0,0,0,,But he will be available\Nmaybe later this morning?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:03.45,1:01:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, the telegram is\Nactually all scrambled.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:07.66,1:01:10.25,Default,,0,0,0,,It's actually from Thompson,\Nnot to him.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:10.46,1:01:13.92,Default,,0,0,0,,All right?\NNow, I've got to go.\NI've gotta get to the race.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:14.00,1:01:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,But there's no hurry.\NThe race is over.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:15.92,1:01:16.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Not for me.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:17.05,1:01:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, let's have lunch !
Dialogue: 0,1:01:20.39,1:01:22.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Righty-o, man. Righty-o.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:23.60,1:01:26.72,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Now, the bricks\Nlay on Grand Street
Dialogue: 0,1:01:26.81,1:01:31.89,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: Jesus.\NBad waves of paranoia.\NMadness. Fear and loathing.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:32.86,1:01:35.11,Default,,0,0,0,,lntolerable vibrations\Nin this place.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:35.61,1:01:40.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out.\NThe weasels were closing in.\Nl could smell the ugly brutes.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:41.95,1:01:43.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Do me one last favor, Lord.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:43.82,1:01:45.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Just give me five more\Nhigh-speed hours
Dialogue: 0,1:01:45.45,1:01:47.20,Default,,0,0,0,,before You bring\Nthe hammer down.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:47.29,1:01:50.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Just let me get rid\Nof this goddamn car\Nand off this horrible desert.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:51.96,1:01:54.63,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Oh, Mama
Dialogue: 0,1:01:55.63,1:01:58.55,Default,,0,0,0,,ls this really the end?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:58.63,1:01:59.88,Default,,0,0,0,,To be stuck inside of Mobile
Dialogue: 0,1:01:59.97,1:02:01.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you evil bastard.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:01.13,1:02:02.22,Default,,0,0,0,,With the Memphis blues again
Dialogue: 0,1:02:02.30,1:02:04.22,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Your work.\NYou better take care of me,\NLord.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:04.34,1:02:07.47,Default,,0,0,0,,(POLICE SIREN WAILING)\NIf You don't, You're gonna\Nhave me on Your hands.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:17.15,1:02:18.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Pull over!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:18.48,1:02:19.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!\NPull over!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:19.61,1:02:20.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning. How are you?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:20.78,1:02:22.74,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, man.\NDoing very well.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:25.45,1:02:28.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Few people understand\Nthe psychology of dealing\Nwith a highway traffic cop.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:28.87,1:02:31.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Your normal speeder will panic\Nand immediately pull over\Nto the side.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:32.54,1:02:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,This is wrong. lt arouses\Ncontempt in the cop heart.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:37.00,1:02:40.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Make the bastard chase you.\NHe will follow.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:40.55,1:02:41.97,Default,,0,0,0,,But he won't know what to\Nmake of your blinker signal
Dialogue: 0,1:02:42.05,1:02:43.84,Default,,0,0,0,,that says you're\Nabout to turn right.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:44.47,1:02:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,This is to let him know\Nyou're pulling off for\Na proper place to talk.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:48.89,1:02:50.43,Default,,0,0,0,,lt'll take him\Na moment to realize
Dialogue: 0,1:02:50.52,1:02:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,that he's about to make\Na 1 80-degree turn, at speed.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:53.56,1:02:57.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But you will be ready for him.\NBrace for the "G"s.\NFast heel-toe work.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:58.07,1:02:59.69,Default,,0,0,0,,COP: Shit! Shit!
Dialogue: 0,1:03:00.36,1:03:02.28,Default,,0,0,0,,(TIRES SCREECHING)
Dialogue: 0,1:03:05.20,1:03:06.82,Default,,0,0,0,,(SIREN WAILING)
Dialogue: 0,1:03:11.04,1:03:12.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi. How are you?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:16.12,1:03:18.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Just what in the hell\Ndid you think\Nyou were doing?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:19.05,1:03:21.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanna know.\NLet me see your license.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:22.63,1:03:24.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah, of course.\NThere you are.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:28.89,1:03:30.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my gosh.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:35.27,1:03:36.48,Default,,0,0,0,,It's me.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:38.23,1:03:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,May I please have that?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:40.98,1:03:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\Nl knew l was fucked.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:49.83,1:03:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,See you have\Ntwo cases of beer,\Na basket of grapefruit,
Dialogue: 0,1:03:53.58,1:03:55.75,Default,,0,0,0,,stack of T-shirts and towels,\Nlight bulbs.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:57.71,1:03:59.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You realize what you did\Nwhen you drive like that?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:59.59,1:04:02.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I know. I'm guilty.\NI understand that.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:02.42,1:04:04.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew it was a crime.\NI did it anyway.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:04.88,1:04:06.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit, why argue?\NI'm a fucking criminal.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:06.55,1:04:07.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at me.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:08.47,1:04:10.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You have a strange attitude.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:10.43,1:04:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:12.43,1:04:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, I have a feeling\Nyou need to take a nap.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:17.10,1:04:19.27,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a rest area\Njust up ahead.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:19.36,1:04:22.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like you to\Ngo up there, pull over\Nand get a few hours' sleep.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:22.73,1:04:24.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not gonna help me.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:24.78,1:04:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been awake for too long,\Nthree or four nights, maybe.\NCan't even remember.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:28.03,1:04:30.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I go to sleep now,\NI'm dead for 20 hours.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:32.37,1:04:35.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you carrying\Ntwo cases of soap for, son?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:35.70,1:04:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanna stay clean.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:38.83,1:04:39.96,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:41.54,1:04:42.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's how it is.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:43.13,1:04:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What I put in my book,\Nas of noon,
Dialogue: 0,1:04:45.97,1:04:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,is that I apprehended you\Nfor driving too fast.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:49.97,1:04:53.22,Default,,0,0,0,,(HUMMING)\NI advised you to proceed\Nto the next rest area. . . Stop!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:57.81,1:05:03.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I advised you to proceed\Nto the next rest area, your\Nstated destination, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:05.44,1:05:07.11,Default,,0,0,0,,And take a long nap.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:08.99,1:05:10.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Do I make myself clear?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:11.53,1:05:14.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, how far is Baker?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:14.74,1:05:18.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I was sort of hoping to,\NI don't know,\Nstop there for lunch.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:19.46,1:05:20.100,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not my jurisdiction.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:21.46,1:05:24.42,Default,,0,0,0,,City limits end 2.2 miles\Nbeyond the rest area.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:25.38,1:05:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you make it that far?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:27.30,1:05:28.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll try.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:29.43,1:05:33.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been wanting to go\Nto Baker for a long time.\NYeah. Heard a lot about it.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:35.56,1:05:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Excellent seafood.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:39.35,1:05:44.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, I'm thinking,\Na guy with your kind of mind\Nought to try the land-crab.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:45.69,1:05:47.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Excellent seafood.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:47.15,1:05:48.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Land-crab.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:49.07,1:05:51.28,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. Why not?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:52.36,1:05:54.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks for the tip.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:54.78,1:05:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at me in the eyes.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:00.21,1:06:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything all right?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:05.38,1:06:07.88,Default,,0,0,0,,May I have a little kiss\Nbefore you go?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:09.38,1:06:10.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm very lonely here.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:12.76,1:06:15.80,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Oh, Mama
Dialogue: 0,1:06:15.89,1:06:18.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Can this really be the end?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:19.22,1:06:22.89,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: I feIt raped.\NThe pig had done me\Non all fronts.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:23.14,1:06:26.48,Default,,0,0,0,,And now he was going off\Nto chuckle about it on\Nthe west side of town,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:26.57,1:06:28.57,Default,,0,0,0,,waiting for me\Nto make a run for L.A.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:30.03,1:06:31.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, yes, Officer.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:31.20,1:06:33.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course l'll take advantage\Nof that rest area.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:33.28,1:06:36.66,Default,,0,0,0,,And l can't tell you how\Ngrateful l am for this break\Nyou wanna give me.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:37.87,1:06:39.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Get a grip, man.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:40.95,1:06:43.58,Default,,0,0,0,,lf l boom straight for L.A.\Nhe'll bust me for sure.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:44.75,1:06:45.96,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:46.59,1:06:48.42,Default,,0,0,0,,This was not the time\Nfor a showdown.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:50.51,1:06:52.26,Default,,0,0,0,,This was Death Valley.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:52.84,1:06:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,(GASPING)
Dialogue: 0,1:06:55.22,1:06:57.09,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE: Oh, fuck!
Dialogue: 0,1:06:57.68,1:07:01.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Sweet Jesus, it's him.\NOh, my God !
Dialogue: 0,1:07:03.39,1:07:05.39,Default,,0,0,0,,(HUMMING)
Dialogue: 0,1:07:05.90,1:07:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,(ENGINE STALLING)
Dialogue: 0,1:07:07.69,1:07:10.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit! Come on,\Nyou fucking bastard.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:10.94,1:07:14.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God. Oh, God. Oh, God.\NI've got to go. I've got to. . .
Dialogue: 0,1:07:17.57,1:07:19.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, they've nailed me,\Ngoddamn it.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:19.41,1:07:21.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm trapped in\Nsome stinking desert\Ncrossroads called Baker.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:21.95,1:07:23.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't have much time, man.\NThe fuckers are closing in.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:23.83,1:07:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll hunt me down\Nlike a fucking beast.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:26.00,1:07:27.71,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO:\NYou sound a little paranoid.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:27.79,1:07:30.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I need a fucking lawyer\Nimmediately!
Dialogue: 0,1:07:30.13,1:07:32.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing in Baker?\NDidn't you get my telegram?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:32.97,1:07:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What telegram,\Nyou worthless bastard?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:36.09,1:07:37.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll cripple your ass\Nfor this.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:37.76,1:07:40.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You brainless scumbag,\Nyou're supposed to be\Nin Vegas.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:40.93,1:07:43.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I rented a suite\Nat the Flamingo.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:43.35,1:07:47.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You're supposed to be\Ncovering the National District\NAttorney's conference.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:47.56,1:07:50.40,Default,,0,0,0,,l made all the reservations.\NEverything is arranged.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:51.28,1:07:54.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, what the fuck are you\Ndoing out there in the\Nmiddle of the desert?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:55.45,1:07:58.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing. Never mind.\NIt's all a big joke.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:58.66,1:08:02.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm actually. . .\NI'm poolside at the\NFlamingo right now,
Dialogue: 0,1:08:02.20,1:08:04.95,Default,,0,0,0,,talking through a portable\Nphone some dwarf brought\Nout from the casino.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:05.04,1:08:06.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah,\NI have total credit here.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:06.83,1:08:09.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't come anywhere near\Nthis place, you bastard.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:09.42,1:08:10.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Foreigners\Naren't welcome here.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:12.80,1:08:15.72,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NWell, this is\Nhow the world works.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:16.51,1:08:19.43,Default,,0,0,0,,All energy flows\Naccording to the whims\Nof the Great Magnet.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:20.93,1:08:22.97,Default,,0,0,0,,What a fool l was to defy him.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:23.72,1:08:27.02,Default,,0,0,0,,l was going back to Vegas.\Nl had no choice.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:27.10,1:08:28.19,Default,,0,0,0,,(GUN FIRING)
Dialogue: 0,1:08:30.19,1:08:32.15,Default,,0,0,0,,l had to get rid of the Shark.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:32.32,1:08:36.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Too many people\Nmight recognize it,\Nespecially the Vegas police.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:37.95,1:08:40.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Luckily, my credit card\Nwas still technically valid.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:41.87,1:08:44.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Now this was\Na superior machine.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:45.20,1:08:48.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Ten grand worth\Nof gimmicks and\Nhigh-priced special effects.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:49.17,1:08:52.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The rear windows leapt up\Nwith a touch like\Nfrogs in a dynamite pond.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:53.42,1:08:56.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The dashboard was\Nfull of esoteric lights\Nand dials and meters
Dialogue: 0,1:08:56.30,1:08:58.38,Default,,0,0,0,,that l would\Nnever understand.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:59.39,1:09:01.64,Default,,0,0,0,,lf the pigs were\Ngathering in Vegas,
Dialogue: 0,1:09:01.72,1:09:04.39,Default,,0,0,0,,l felt the drug culture\Nshould be represented as well.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:05.02,1:09:07.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And there was a certain\Nbent appeal in the notion\Nof running a savage burn
Dialogue: 0,1:09:07.94,1:09:09.73,Default,,0,0,0,,on one Las Vegas hotel,
Dialogue: 0,1:09:09.81,1:09:12.90,Default,,0,0,0,,and then just\Nwheeling across town\Nand checking into another.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:13.40,1:09:16.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Me and 1 ,000 ranking cops\Nfrom all over America.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:16.78,1:09:19.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not move confidently\Ninto their midst?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:19.90,1:09:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Welcome to\Nthe Flamingo Hotel, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:22.20,1:09:24.07,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTING)
Dialogue: 0,1:09:25.58,1:09:28.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir?\NYeah, hi. Right. Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:28.25,1:09:30.33,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING)\NLet me stay in your arms
Dialogue: 0,1:09:30.42,1:09:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,l'm addicted to your charms
Dialogue: 0,1:09:33.13,1:09:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You're getting to be\Na habit with me
Dialogue: 0,1:09:38.17,1:09:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,l used to think your love\Nwas something that l
Dialogue: 0,1:09:41.72,1:09:43.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Could take
Dialogue: 0,1:09:43.22,1:09:44.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Or leave alone
Dialogue: 0,1:09:44.43,1:09:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: My arrivaI\Nwas badly timed.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:47.10,1:09:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) But now I couIdn't\Ndo without my supply
Dialogue: 0,1:09:50.94,1:09:54.06,Default,,0,0,0,,l need you for my own
Dialogue: 0,1:10:01.11,1:10:02.78,Default,,0,0,0,,This here model is one\Nthat we had to use
Dialogue: 0,1:10:02.86,1:10:06.16,Default,,0,0,0,,when we took on\Nthem little peckerheads\Ndown there at Kent State.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:07.04,1:10:08.74,Default,,0,0,0,,And this baby here. . .
Dialogue: 0,1:10:11.62,1:10:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a police chief\Nfrom Michigan.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:14.29,1:10:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, fella,\NI have explained to you.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:16.25,1:10:21.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I have this postcard\Nwhich says that I have\Na reservation in this hotel.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:21.84,1:10:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm very sorry, sir,\Nbut you're on the late list.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:25.64,1:10:29.52,Default,,0,0,0,,And so, your reservation\Nhas been transferred to. . .\NIt's okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:30.31,1:10:36.27,Default,,0,0,0,,. . .the Moonlight Motel\Nwhich is just out on\NParadise Boulevard.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:36.36,1:10:38.57,Default,,0,0,0,,We've already paid\Nfor our goddamn room !
Dialogue: 0,1:10:38.65,1:10:40.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, it's actually a very\Nfine place of lodging,
Dialogue: 0,1:10:40.99,1:10:45.24,Default,,0,0,0,,and it's only\N1 6 blocks from here.\NIt has a pool, sauna, steam.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:45.32,1:10:47.20,Default,,0,0,0,,You listen to me,\Nyou filthy little faggot!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:47.28,1:10:49.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I want a manager down here,\Nnow, now!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:49.99,1:10:52.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, because I'm sick of\Nlistening to your dog shit!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:52.87,1:10:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I am very sorry, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:56.25,1:10:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Get off of me!\NGet away from me!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:58.00,1:10:59.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Can I call you a cab?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:59.21,1:11:01.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure, and I'll call you\Na cocksucker!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:01.26,1:11:04.38,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: Of course,\Nl could hear what the\Nclerk was really saying.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:04.64,1:11:07.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen,\Nyou fuzzy little shithead !
Dialogue: 0,1:11:08.18,1:11:10.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been fucked around\Nin my time
Dialogue: 0,1:11:10.60,1:11:12.81,Default,,0,0,0,,by a fairly good cross section
Dialogue: 0,1:11:12.89,1:11:16.02,Default,,0,0,0,,of mean-tempered,\Nrule-crazy cops.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:16.10,1:11:19.36,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, it's my turn.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:21.23,1:11:25.32,Default,,0,0,0,,So fuck you, Officer.\NI'm in charge.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:25.57,1:11:27.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, listen,\NI really hate to interrupt,
Dialogue: 0,1:11:27.91,1:11:30.12,Default,,0,0,0,,but I wonder if I could\Njust slide on through\Nand get out of your way.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:30.20,1:11:31.79,Default,,0,0,0,,The name is Duke. Raoul Duke.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:31.87,1:11:34.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I think my attorney\Nmade the reservations.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:34.25,1:11:35.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Duke, Raoul.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:35.87,1:11:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Certainly, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:37.50,1:11:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,My bags. . . My bags are\Nout there in that white\NCadillac convertible there.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:41.51,1:11:43.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe somebody could\Nbring it to the room for me.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:43.47,1:11:48.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, let me get\Na quart of Wild Turkey,
Dialogue: 0,1:11:48.39,1:11:51.93,Default,,0,0,0,,two-fifths of Bacardi,\Nsome ice for the room,\Nand let's see. . .
Dialogue: 0,1:11:52.02,1:11:53.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You just calm down !
Dialogue: 0,1:11:53.18,1:11:55.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit, let's try\Nsome lime chunks.\NWhat do you think?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:55.64,1:11:56.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I say okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:58.69,1:12:00.19,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't worry\Nabout a thing.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:00.27,1:12:01.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, calm down.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:01.40,1:12:04.74,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't hesitate\Nto call me, Sven.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:05.61,1:12:06.82,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Sven.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:06.90,1:12:08.11,Default,,0,0,0,,(WAILING)
Dialogue: 0,1:12:08.20,1:12:09.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:09.41,1:12:10.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You. . . You. . .
Dialogue: 0,1:12:10.87,1:12:13.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I know, I know, I know.\NIt's hideous.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:13.24,1:12:15.12,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna be fine, though.\NYou're doing well.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:16.16,1:12:18.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll see you later. Wait.\NDon't touch it.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:18.12,1:12:20.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Good night. Pardon me.\NBye, Sven.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:20.71,1:12:22.09,Default,,0,0,0,,(CRYING)
Dialogue: 0,1:12:22.63,1:12:25.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Look what you did !\NLook what you did !
Dialogue: 0,1:12:26.01,1:12:29.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn you,\Nwe wouldn't stay in this\Nhotel if you begged us!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:29.80,1:12:33.43,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Magic moments
Dialogue: 0,1:12:34.14,1:12:38.27,Default,,0,0,0,,When two hearts are caring
Dialogue: 0,1:12:38.81,1:12:43.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Magic moments
Dialogue: 0,1:12:43.57,1:12:46.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Memories we've been sharing
Dialogue: 0,1:12:46.74,1:12:49.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Home, sweet home. Whoa.\NWhat kind of sick shit. . .
Dialogue: 0,1:12:49.66,1:12:51.37,Default,,0,0,0,,(LUCY GRUNTING)\NOh, shit!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:53.37,1:12:55.12,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTING)\NShit. What the fuck?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:55.58,1:12:57.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop, stop, stop.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:57.21,1:12:58.100,Default,,0,0,0,,She's biting my leg off!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:59.08,1:13:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,You degenerate pig. Please!
Dialogue: 0,1:13:01.84,1:13:03.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't be helped.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:03.21,1:13:04.21,Default,,0,0,0,,My fucking leg !
Dialogue: 0,1:13:04.30,1:13:06.80,Default,,0,0,0,,That's "Lucy In The Sky\NWith Diamonds."
Dialogue: 0,1:13:07.59,1:13:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Lucy, be cool,\Ngoddamn it.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:10.84,1:13:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember what happened\Nat the airport, okay?\NCome on.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:14.31,1:13:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,(LUCY WHIMPERS)
Dialogue: 0,1:13:17.77,1:13:21.23,Default,,0,0,0,,No more of that, okay?\NThat's my client, Lucy.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:21.77,1:13:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,That's Mr. Duke,\Nthe famous journalist.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:25.57,1:13:27.48,Default,,0,0,0,,He's paying for this suite,\NLucy.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:28.44,1:13:29.86,Default,,0,0,0,,He's on our side.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:30.82,1:13:32.78,Default,,0,0,0,,He loves artists.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:33.70,1:13:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Lucy paints portraits\Nof Barbra Streisand.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:39.08,1:13:40.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:41.58,1:13:43.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I drew these from TV.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:44.25,1:13:45.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Really.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:46.17,1:13:48.80,Default,,0,0,0,,She came all the way down. . .
Dialogue: 0,1:13:49.34,1:13:51.84,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the name\Nof that town?\NMontana.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:51.93,1:13:55.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Montana.\NJust to give these\Nportraits to Barbra.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:57.35,1:14:00.98,Default,,0,0,0,,We're going over to\Nthe Americana tonight\Nto meet her backstage.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:01.19,1:14:05.98,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: I desperateIy\Nneeded peace, rest, sanctuary.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:07.11,1:14:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,l hadn't counted on this,\Nfinding my attorney on acid
Dialogue: 0,1:14:10.07,1:14:12.74,Default,,0,0,0,,and locked into some kind\Nof preternatural courtship.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:13.03,1:14:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Well.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:15.53,1:14:19.37,Default,,0,0,0,,They must have brought\Nthe car around by now.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:19.100,1:14:23.17,Default,,0,0,0,,So why don't
Dialogue: 0,1:14:24.63,1:14:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,ou-yay and I-ay
Dialogue: 0,1:14:29.17,1:14:31.34,Default,,0,0,0,,o-gay and et-gay the
Dialogue: 0,1:14:33.01,1:14:36.60,Default,,0,0,0,,uff-stay out of the unk-tray.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:42.90,1:14:44.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Absolutely. Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:45.27,1:14:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's get the stuff.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:47.86,1:14:49.44,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll be right back, Lucy.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:50.90,1:14:52.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me a kiss?\NOne kiss, one kiss.\NNo.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:53.07,1:14:54.32,Default,,0,0,0,,LUCY: No.\NGONZO: One kiss.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:54.41,1:14:55.53,Default,,0,0,0,,No.\NWhy not?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:55.62,1:14:57.57,Default,,0,0,0,,No.\NOkay.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:03.100,1:15:05.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't answer the phone.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:13.47,1:15:14.80,Default,,0,0,0,,God bless.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:17.93,1:15:20.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, what are your plans?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:21.23,1:15:22.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Plans?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:22.73,1:15:24.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The child in the bedroom.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:24.77,1:15:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Lucy.\NI met her on the plane.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:30.82,1:15:33.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\NShe's a religious freak.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:34.57,1:15:37.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I gave her a cap\Nbefore I realized. . .
