Dialogue: 0,1:25:16.11,1:25:17.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:17.86,1:25:21.53,Default,,0,0,0,,She's my problem.\NI'll call her,\NI'll get her off our backs.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:21.62,1:25:22.99,Default,,0,0,0,,It's gone too fucking far.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:23.08,1:25:25.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I'll take that\Ninto consideration.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:25.37,1:25:26.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Relax.\NRelax!
Dialogue: 0,1:25:26.100,1:25:28.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me handle this.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:32.42,1:25:33.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are my shoes?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:33.63,1:25:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The Americana Hotel.\NWhat did you do\Nwith my goddamn shoes?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:35.51,1:25:37.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Room 1 600, please.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:37.22,1:25:41.43,Default,,0,0,0,,As your attorney, I advise you\Nto take a hit out\Nof the little brown bottle
Dialogue: 0,1:25:41.51,1:25:43.30,Default,,0,0,0,,in my shaving kit.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:44.06,1:25:45.72,Default,,0,0,0,,You won't need much.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:47.68,1:25:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Just a tiny taste.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:49.73,1:25:53.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's have it.\NAh, there it is.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:57.44,1:25:59.44,Default,,0,0,0,,What is this shit?\NThat stuff
Dialogue: 0,1:25:59.74,1:26:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,makes pure mescaline\Nseem like ginger beer, man.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:05.91,1:26:07.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Adrenochrome.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:07.74,1:26:09.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Adrenochrome? Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:09.58,1:26:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,(PHONE RINGS)
Dialogue: 0,1:26:17.13,1:26:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:20.26,1:26:22.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, Lucy. God bless.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:22.55,1:26:23.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:23.93,1:26:25.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's me.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:25.72,1:26:29.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell, no,\NI taught the bastard a lesson\Nhe'll never forget.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:29.93,1:26:33.10,Default,,0,0,0,,What? No, not dead.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:33.27,1:26:36.48,Default,,0,0,0,,But he won't be bothering\Nanybody for a while.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:36.57,1:26:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I left him out there.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:38.94,1:26:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I stomped him.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:41.32,1:26:43.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I pulled all his teeth out.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:43.11,1:26:44.66,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\Nl remember thinking,\N"Jesus.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:44.74,1:26:47.33,Default,,0,0,0,,"What a terrible thing\Nto lay on somebody\Nwith a head full of acid."
Dialogue: 0,1:26:47.41,1:26:49.16,Default,,0,0,0,,But we have a problem.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:49.24,1:26:51.58,Default,,0,0,0,,That bastard cashed\Na bad check downstairs
Dialogue: 0,1:26:51.66,1:26:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,and gave you as a reference.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:53.79,1:26:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll be\Nlooking for both of you.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:56.67,1:27:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I know,\NLucy, but you can't\Njudge a book by its cover.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:00.80,1:27:03.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Some people are\Njust basically rotten.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:05.47,1:27:07.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyway, the last thing\Nin the world you wanna do
Dialogue: 0,1:27:07.51,1:27:09.85,Default,,0,0,0,,is call this hotel again.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:10.31,1:27:12.31,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll trace the call,\Nput you straight behind bars.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:12.39,1:27:13.64,Default,,0,0,0,,(BABBLING)
Dialogue: 0,1:27:14.56,1:27:16.81,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I'm moving\Nto the Tropicana right away.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:19.15,1:27:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:20.36,1:27:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll use a different name.\NI'll let you know what it is.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:28.12,1:27:29.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I gotta get off.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:30.70,1:27:33.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Probably have this phone\Ntapped, baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:33.96,1:27:35.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I know,\Nit was horrible,\Nbut it's all over now.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:36.08,1:27:37.29,Default,,0,0,0,,(BANGING)
Dialogue: 0,1:27:38.04,1:27:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God.\NThere's someone at the door.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:40.80,1:27:41.76,Default,,0,0,0,,(SQUEALING)
Dialogue: 0,1:27:41.84,1:27:43.22,Default,,0,0,0,,(WHISPERING)\NThere's someone at the door.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:43.30,1:27:44.55,Default,,0,0,0,,(BANGING)
Dialogue: 0,1:27:45.72,1:27:47.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Christ! Hey!
Dialogue: 0,1:27:48.39,1:27:51.18,Default,,0,0,0,,No! I'm innocent!\NIt was Duke!
Dialogue: 0,1:27:51.27,1:27:54.56,Default,,0,0,0,,It was Duke! Lucy! Lucy!
Dialogue: 0,1:27:54.64,1:27:57.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I love you ! I love you !
Dialogue: 0,1:27:57.19,1:27:58.56,Default,,0,0,0,,(SCREAMING)
Dialogue: 0,1:28:03.53,1:28:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't put that thing on me!
Dialogue: 0,1:28:04.95,1:28:06.53,Default,,0,0,0,,(SCREAMING)
Dialogue: 0,1:28:11.62,1:28:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoo. Oh.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:15.16,1:28:16.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Well. . .
Dialogue: 0,1:28:18.29,1:28:20.38,Default,,0,0,0,,That's that.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:20.63,1:28:21.63,Default,,0,0,0,,(GURGLING)
Dialogue: 0,1:28:21.71,1:28:24.59,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the last we should\Nbe hearing from Lucy, man.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:25.51,1:28:26.63,Default,,0,0,0,,(EXHALES)
Dialogue: 0,1:28:28.43,1:28:32.35,Default,,0,0,0,,She's probably\Nstuffing herself down\Nthe incinerator about now.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:35.98,1:28:37.60,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what we need?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:37.69,1:28:39.27,Default,,0,0,0,,We need some opium.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:48.32,1:28:49.41,Default,,0,0,0,,(GURGLING)
Dialogue: 0,1:28:51.24,1:28:53.28,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: I remember\Nslumping on the bed.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:53.37,1:28:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,His performance\Nhad given me a bad jolt.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:55.95,1:28:58.71,Default,,0,0,0,,For a moment, l thought\Nhis mind had snapped,
Dialogue: 0,1:28:58.79,1:29:02.00,Default,,0,0,0,,that he actually believed\Nhe was being attacked\Nby invisible enemies.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:02.42,1:29:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,But the room was quiet again.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:06.88,1:29:08.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Where'd you get this?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:08.89,1:29:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind.\NIt's absolutely pure.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:12.68,1:29:15.18,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of monster client\Nhave you hooked up\Nwith this time?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:15.27,1:29:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Satanism freak.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:17.60,1:29:19.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I think there's only\None source for this stuff,
Dialogue: 0,1:29:19.35,1:29:22.81,Default,,0,0,0,,the adrenaline gland
Dialogue: 0,1:29:22.90,1:29:26.15,Default,,0,0,0,,from a living human body.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:26.57,1:29:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:28.15,1:29:30.36,Default,,0,0,0,,The guy didn't have\Nany cash to pay me.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:30.99,1:29:34.99,Default,,0,0,0,,He offered me human blood,\Nsaid it would take me higher\Nthan I'd ever been in my life.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:35.58,1:29:37.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought\Nhe was kidding.\NOh.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:37.62,1:29:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,So I told him I'd just\Nas soon have an ounce\Nor so of pure adrenochrome.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:42.63,1:29:45.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Or maybe just\Na fresh adrenaline gland
Dialogue: 0,1:29:45.51,1:29:46.96,Default,,0,0,0,,to chew on.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:47.13,1:29:49.97,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: I couId\Nalready feel the stuff\Nworking on me.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:50.09,1:29:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,The first wave felt\Nlike a combination\Nof mescaline and methedrine.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:54.47,1:29:56.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe l should take a swim,\Nl thought.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:56.97,1:29:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:00.69,1:30:05.36,Default,,0,0,0,,They nailed this guy\Nfor child molesting.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:06.11,1:30:07.94,Default,,0,0,0,,He swore he didn't do it.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:08.03,1:30:11.95,Default,,0,0,0,,"Why should I fuck\Nwith children?" he said.\N"They're too small."
Dialogue: 0,1:30:12.03,1:30:13.11,Default,,0,0,0,,(WHINING)
Dialogue: 0,1:30:13.20,1:30:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Christ, what could I say?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:14.49,1:30:17.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Even a goddamn werewolf\Nis entitled to legal counsel.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:18.83,1:30:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't dare to\Nturn the creep down.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:23.96,1:30:27.09,Default,,0,0,0,,He might have\Npicked up a letter opener\Nand gone after my
Dialogue: 0,1:30:28.13,1:30:29.21,Default,,0,0,0,,pineal gland.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:30.76,1:30:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You know?\NYeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:32.68,1:30:34.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Crazy.\NWhy not?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:35.18,1:30:38.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit. We should get\Nsome of that.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:38.60,1:30:40.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Just
Dialogue: 0,1:30:40.18,1:30:41.81,Default,,0,0,0,,eat a big handful\Nand see what happens.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:42.73,1:30:44.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Some of what?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:46.02,1:30:47.11,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTING)
Dialogue: 0,1:30:47.19,1:30:48.40,Default,,0,0,0,,(SNIFFING)
Dialogue: 0,1:30:48.82,1:30:50.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Extract of pineal.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:50.82,1:30:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure, that's a good idea.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:53.53,1:30:55.11,Default,,0,0,0,,One whiff of that stuff\Nwill turn you
Dialogue: 0,1:30:55.20,1:30:58.12,Default,,0,0,0,,into something\Nout of a goddamn
Dialogue: 0,1:30:59.45,1:31:01.87,Default,,0,0,0,,medical encyclopedia, man.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:04.08,1:31:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Beautiful fucking tits.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:06.54,1:31:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Man, your head would swell up\Nlike a watermelon.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:09.80,1:31:12.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd gain about\N1 00 pounds in two hours.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:12.47,1:31:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:14.30,1:31:16.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Grow claws, bleeding warts.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:16.89,1:31:18.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:18.51,1:31:22.31,Default,,0,0,0,,And then you'd notice\Nabout six huge, hairy tits
Dialogue: 0,1:31:22.39,1:31:24.48,Default,,0,0,0,,swelling up on your back.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:24.81,1:31:26.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Fantastic!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:26.69,1:31:28.40,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd go blind.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:30.19,1:31:32.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Your body would turn to wax.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:33.07,1:31:35.15,Default,,0,0,0,,They'd have to put you\Nin a wheelbarrow.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:35.24,1:31:37.24,Default,,0,0,0,,And when you scream for help,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:37.41,1:31:39.70,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll sound like a raccoon.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:40.16,1:31:41.54,Default,,0,0,0,,(WHIMPERING)
Dialogue: 0,1:31:41.87,1:31:44.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Man, I'll try\Njust about anything,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:44.87,1:31:48.08,Default,,0,0,0,,but I'd never in hell\Ntouch a pineal gland.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:48.17,1:31:51.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Finish the fucking story, man !
Dialogue: 0,1:31:51.17,1:31:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened?\NWhat about the glands?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:54.72,1:31:58.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Jesus, that stuff\Ngot right on top of you,\Ndidn't it?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:58.26,1:32:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at your face.\NYou're about to explode.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:09.19,1:32:10.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe you could just
Dialogue: 0,1:32:12.82,1:32:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,shove me into the pool.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:14.95,1:32:17.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Man, if I put you\Nin the pool right now,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:17.24,1:32:19.53,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll sink\Nlike a goddamn stone.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:20.20,1:32:23.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You took too much, man.\NYou took too much. Too much.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:25.08,1:32:26.25,Default,,0,0,0,,(GURGLING)
Dialogue: 0,1:32:27.04,1:32:28.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't try and fight it.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:28.63,1:32:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll get brain bubbles,\Nstrokes, aneurysms.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:32.46,1:32:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll just wither up\Nand die.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:35.88,1:32:37.97,Default,,0,0,0,,(DUKE MUTTERING INCOHERENTLY)
Dialogue: 0,1:32:38.51,1:32:40.35,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN ON T.V. : They continue\Nkilling innocent people!
Dialogue: 0,1:32:40.43,1:32:44.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Allowing the hopes\Nfor peace and freedom\Nof millions of people
Dialogue: 0,1:32:44.31,1:32:45.81,Default,,0,0,0,,to be suffocated.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:46.27,1:32:49.31,Default,,0,0,0,,So tonight, to you,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:49.77,1:32:52.15,Default,,0,0,0,,the great silent majority...
Dialogue: 0,1:32:52.32,1:32:53.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Sacrifice. Sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:54.07,1:32:55.94,Default,,0,0,0,,(ECHOING) Sacrifice.\NSacrifice. Sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:56.03,1:32:59.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Sacrifice. Sacrifice.\NSacrifice. Sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:59.11,1:33:00.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:06.100,1:33:12.67,Default,,0,0,0,,WOMAN:\Nl feel the cottonwood\Nwhispering above
Dialogue: 0,1:33:13.30,1:33:16.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Tammy, Tammy
Dialogue: 0,1:33:17.26,1:33:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,(MOANING)\NTammy's in love
Dialogue: 0,1:33:21.97,1:33:23.68,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: What kind\Nof rat-bastard psychotic
Dialogue: 0,1:33:23.76,1:33:26.43,Default,,0,0,0,,would play that song\Nright now, at this moment?
Dialogue: 0,1:33:27.85,1:33:30.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Tammy, Tammy
Dialogue: 0,1:33:30.73,1:33:32.73,Default,,0,0,0,,When l came to,
Dialogue: 0,1:33:32.98,1:33:36.19,Default,,0,0,0,,the general back-alley\Nambience of the suite\Nwas so rotten,
Dialogue: 0,1:33:36.40,1:33:38.36,Default,,0,0,0,,so incredibly foul.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:40.36,1:33:43.28,Default,,0,0,0,,How long had l been\Nlying there?
Dialogue: 0,1:33:43.45,1:33:45.62,Default,,0,0,0,,All these signs of violence.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:46.37,1:33:47.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What had happened?
Dialogue: 0,1:33:47.50,1:33:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,(INSECT BUZZING)
Dialogue: 0,1:33:48.71,1:33:50.66,Default,,0,0,0,,There was evidence\Nin this room of excessive\Nconsumption
Dialogue: 0,1:33:50.75,1:33:56.09,Default,,0,0,0,,of almost every type of drug\Nknown to civilized man\Nsince 1 544 A.D.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:59.38,1:34:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,(COUGHING)
Dialogue: 0,1:34:03.05,1:34:04.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, ah, Debbie.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:05.39,1:34:06.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank God.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:07.27,1:34:10.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Debbie. Hmm? Look.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:12.77,1:34:14.90,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NWhat kind of addict would\Nneed all these coconut husks
Dialogue: 0,1:34:14.98,1:34:17.07,Default,,0,0,0,,and crushed honeydew rinds?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:17.23,1:34:20.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Would the presence of junkies\Naccount for all these\Nuneaten French fries?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:20.74,1:34:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,These puddles of glazed\Nketchup on the bureau?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:23.78,1:34:25.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe so.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:26.12,1:34:27.66,Default,,0,0,0,,But then why all this booze
Dialogue: 0,1:34:28.29,1:34:29.100,Default,,0,0,0,,and these crude\Npornographic photos
Dialogue: 0,1:34:30.08,1:34:32.96,Default,,0,0,0,,smeared with mustard\Nthat had dried to a hard,\Nyellow crust?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:33.04,1:34:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,These were not\Nthe hoofprints of your\Nnormal God-fearing junkie.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:36.42,1:34:39.09,Default,,0,0,0,,lt was too savage,\Ntoo aggressive.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:39.17,1:34:40.92,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: Put your hands\Nwhere I can see them.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:41.01,1:34:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,What? What?\NJesus God, man. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:43.84,1:34:46.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Put your hands\Nwhere I can see them.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:46.56,1:34:48.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Put your hands\Nwhere I can see them !
Dialogue: 0,1:34:48.64,1:34:49.68,Default,,0,0,0,,(GROANS)
Dialogue: 0,1:34:49.77,1:34:52.60,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NGrim memories\Nand bad flashbacks.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:53.10,1:34:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Get a grip.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:54.85,1:34:56.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Maintain.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:57.57,1:35:00.98,Default,,0,0,0,,How many nights\Nand weird mornings\Nhad this shit been going on?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:12.29,1:35:13.58,Default,,0,0,0,,(URINATING)
Dialogue: 0,1:35:18.13,1:35:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Something ugly had happened.\Nl was sure of it.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:21.76,1:35:22.84,Default,,0,0,0,,(RETCHING)
Dialogue: 0,1:35:27.26,1:35:30.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is that?\NOh. Shit, that's me.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:32.31,1:35:33.77,Default,,0,0,0,,(MUTTERING)
Dialogue: 0,1:35:34.31,1:35:35.56,Default,,0,0,0,,(WOMAN SCREAMING)
Dialogue: 0,1:35:35.65,1:35:37.31,Default,,0,0,0,,WOMAN: Help me!\NThe fuck!
Dialogue: 0,1:35:37.48,1:35:38.69,Default,,0,0,0,,What the fuck?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:38.77,1:35:39.77,Default,,0,0,0,,(GONZO YELLING)
Dialogue: 0,1:35:39.86,1:35:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, shit.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:41.32,1:35:42.65,Default,,0,0,0,,(WOMAN YELLING)
Dialogue: 0,1:35:44.65,1:35:47.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You're under arrest!\NShe must have\Nused a pass key.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:47.62,1:35:48.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I was polishing my shoes\Nin the closet
Dialogue: 0,1:35:48.99,1:35:50.58,Default,,0,0,0,,when I noticed her\Nsneaking in, so I took her.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:50.66,1:35:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,What made you do it?\NWho paid you off?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:51.100,1:35:53.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Nobody! I'm the maid !
Dialogue: 0,1:35:53.46,1:35:55.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You're just as much\Na part of it as they are.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:55.37,1:35:56.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Part of what?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:56.75,1:35:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The goddamn dope ring.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:58.50,1:36:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You must know\Nwhat's going on\Nin this hotel.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:00.21,1:36:01.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Why do you think we're here?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:01.96,1:36:03.67,Default,,0,0,0,,(STUTTERING)\NI know you're the cops,
Dialogue: 0,1:36:03.80,1:36:06.26,Default,,0,0,0,,but I thought\Nyou were just here\Nfor the convention.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:06.34,1:36:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I swear. All I wanted to do\Nwas clean up the room.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:09.89,1:36:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know\Nanything about no dope.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:12.18,1:36:13.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:13.77,1:36:15.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't try to tell us\Nyou never heard\Nof the Grange Gorman.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:16.02,1:36:18.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I swear to Jesus\NI never heard of that stuff.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:18.86,1:36:20.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe she's telling the truth.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:21.02,1:36:22.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe she's not part of it.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:22.86,1:36:25.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I swear I'm not. I swear.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:28.74,1:36:30.66,Default,,0,0,0,,In that case,\Nmaybe she can help.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:30.74,1:36:33.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes,\NI'll help you all you want.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:33.58,1:36:34.100,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate dope.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:35.54,1:36:36.62,Default,,0,0,0,,So do we.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:36.71,1:36:38.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I think we should\Nput her on the payroll,
Dialogue: 0,1:36:39.08,1:36:40.75,Default,,0,0,0,,see what she comes up with.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:40.84,1:36:42.63,Default,,0,0,0,,You think\Nyou can handle it?\NWhat?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:42.71,1:36:44.84,Default,,0,0,0,,One phone call every day.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:45.09,1:36:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry\Nif it doesn't add up.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:47.01,1:36:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,That's our problem.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:48.22,1:36:49.93,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd pay me for that?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:50.01,1:36:51.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You're damn right we would.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:52.47,1:36:55.56,Default,,0,0,0,,But the first time\Nthat you say anything\Nabout this to anybody
Dialogue: 0,1:36:55.68,1:36:58.44,Default,,0,0,0,,you will go straight to prison\Nfor the rest of your life.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:58.73,1:36:59.85,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:59.94,1:37:01.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Alice.\NProve it!
Dialogue: 0,1:37:02.82,1:37:04.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:04.40,1:37:06.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Just ring Linen Service\Nand ask for Alice.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:06.57,1:37:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Alice.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:11.57,1:37:15.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll be contacted\Nby Inspector Rock,\NArthur Rock.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:16.45,1:37:18.12,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll be posing\Nas a politician,
Dialogue: 0,1:37:18.21,1:37:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,but you'll have no problem\Nrecognizing him.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:19.96,1:37:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right, Inspector Rock\Nwill pay you in cash.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:24.21,1:37:26.26,Default,,0,0,0,,$1 ,000 on the ninth\Nof every month.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:26.42,1:37:29.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Lord ! I'd do just about\Nanything for that.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:29.43,1:37:31.34,Default,,0,0,0,,You and a lot\Nof other people.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:31.43,1:37:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here. The password is,\N"One hand washes the other."
Dialogue: 0,1:37:35.27,1:37:39.14,Default,,0,0,0,,The minute you hear that,\Nyou say, "I fear nothing."
Dialogue: 0,1:37:39.44,1:37:40.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Say it.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:40.90,1:37:42.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I fear nothing.\NSay it again !
Dialogue: 0,1:37:42.23,1:37:43.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I fear nothing !\NVery good.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:43.98,1:37:45.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Get the fuck out of here.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:45.48,1:37:47.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah, listen.\NNice meeting you.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:49.15,1:37:50.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't bother\Nto make up the room.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:50.78,1:37:54.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Just leave a pile of towels\Nand soap outside the door\Nexactly at midnight.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:54.16,1:37:56.74,Default,,0,0,0,,That way we won't\Nhave to risk another
Dialogue: 0,1:37:56.83,1:37:58.41,Default,,0,0,0,,one of these\Nlittle incidents, will we?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:58.50,1:38:00.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever you say, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:00.25,1:38:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank God for decent people.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:02.79,1:38:04.96,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE ON TAPE: Say it again!\NWOMAN: l fear nothing!
Dialogue: 0,1:38:05.50,1:38:06.84,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NTerrible gibberish.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:06.92,1:38:09.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Splintered memories looming up\Nout of the time fog.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:10.13,1:38:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Just press play.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:13.01,1:38:15.01,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE ON TAPE: This is it,\Nthe American Dream.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:15.10,1:38:16.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit!
Dialogue: 0,1:38:16.18,1:38:17.56,Default,,0,0,0,,We're sitting\Non the main nerve right now.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:17.64,1:38:19.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, don't get me started.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:20.02,1:38:23.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The owner always wanted\Nto run away and join\Nthe circus when he was a kid.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:23.86,1:38:26.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Now the son of a bitch\Nowns the circus.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:27.15,1:38:30.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, man,\Na real license to steal.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:30.53,1:38:31.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:31.99,1:38:33.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The American Dream\Ncome true, man.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:33.87,1:38:35.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Pure Horatio Alger.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:36.20,1:38:38.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Welcome\Nto the happy place.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:38.79,1:38:39.91,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTING)
Dialogue: 0,1:38:40.29,1:38:43.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, let's get down\Nto brass tacks here.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:44.38,1:38:46.13,Default,,0,0,0,,How much for the ape?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:46.38,1:38:48.46,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN CHUCKLING:\NHow much you got?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:48.84,1:38:50.92,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE ON TAPE:\NHow much do you think\Nyou'd take for the ape?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:51.18,1:38:53.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Just wait here.\Nl'll be back.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:53.34,1:38:56.47,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: Madness.\Nlt made no sense at all.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:56.56,1:38:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,l desperately\Nneeded the facts.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:59.39,1:39:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,(DUKE YELLING)
Dialogue: 0,1:39:03.69,1:39:05.27,Default,,0,0,0,,(HARD ROCK MUSIC\NPLAYING ON TAPE)
Dialogue: 0,1:39:07.02,1:39:08.90,Default,,0,0,0,,What the fuck is going on?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:08.98,1:39:10.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the ape, man?\NWhere's the ape?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:10.99,1:39:13.36,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN: Forget about it.\NHe attacked an old man.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:13.53,1:39:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Bit off the head\Nof the bartender,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:14.95,1:39:17.66,Default,,0,0,0,,then the cops came\Nand took him away.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:19.33,1:39:21.16,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTING)\NIs that your car?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:22.46,1:39:23.71,Default,,0,0,0,,(SHOUTING)
Dialogue: 0,1:39:26.71,1:39:28.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Somebody stop them !
Dialogue: 0,1:39:28.42,1:39:30.05,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE: You poor fools\Ndon't understand, do you?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:30.13,1:39:32.67,Default,,0,0,0,,This car is property\Nof the World Bank.\NThat money goes to Italy.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:32.76,1:39:35.47,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't put on a circus\Nwithout a tent.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:35.55,1:39:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The top\Nis completely jammed.\NYou're right.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:39.18,1:39:40.56,Default,,0,0,0,,There's something wrong\Nwith the motor.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:40.64,1:39:42.60,Default,,0,0,0,,We're all riders of the storm.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:42.69,1:39:45.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you,\Nyou fucking monkey?\NYou can't do that!
Dialogue: 0,1:39:48.15,1:39:49.82,Default,,0,0,0,,You people voted\Nfor Hubert Humphrey.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:49.90,1:39:51.27,Default,,0,0,0,,And you killed Jesus.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:51.40,1:39:54.19,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE: There was every reason\Nto believe that we'd been\Nheading for trouble,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:54.28,1:39:56.78,Default,,0,0,0,,that we'd pushed\Nour luck a bit too far.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:56.86,1:39:59.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, gosh, shit! God !
Dialogue: 0,1:40:01.79,1:40:03.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Right. Uh. . .
Dialogue: 0,1:40:03.96,1:40:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The possibility
Dialogue: 0,1:40:06.04,1:40:08.79,Default,,0,0,0,,of physical\Nand mental collapse
Dialogue: 0,1:40:09.38,1:40:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,is now very real.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:12.21,1:40:14.13,Default,,0,0,0,,No sympathy for the devil.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:14.72,1:40:16.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep that in mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:16.93,1:40:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, buy the ticket. . .
Dialogue: 0,1:40:19.60,1:40:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, take the ride.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:23.18,1:40:24.48,Default,,0,0,0,,(WEEPING)
Dialogue: 0,1:40:25.98,1:40:27.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, there.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:27.56,1:40:30.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You folks want to\Nbuy some heroin?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:30.57,1:40:31.94,Default,,0,0,0,,(GONZO WEEPING)
Dialogue: 0,1:40:37.45,1:40:39.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, honkies! Goddamn it!
Dialogue: 0,1:40:39.91,1:40:41.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Pull ahead, will you?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:41.91,1:40:45.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to sell you\Nsome pure fucking scag !
Dialogue: 0,1:40:45.46,1:40:48.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Cheap! The real stuff.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:48.12,1:40:51.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I just got back from Vietnam.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:57.22,1:40:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Scag.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:00.64,1:41:03.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to sell you\Nsome pure fucking scag.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:03.97,1:41:06.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit! Fuck!
Dialogue: 0,1:41:07.56,1:41:11.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Now hear me, you bastard !\NPull over! I'll kill you !
Dialogue: 0,1:41:11.48,1:41:12.98,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN ON TAPE:\NPull over! Come on!
Dialogue: 0,1:41:14.69,1:41:16.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, shit. Oh, oh.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:18.11,1:41:19.65,Default,,0,0,0,,(SLOW JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING)
Dialogue: 0,1:41:24.95,1:41:28.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. Let's see here.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:36.42,1:41:40.34,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NThe mentality of Las Vegas\Nis so grossly atavistic
Dialogue: 0,1:41:40.43,1:41:44.10,Default,,0,0,0,,that a really massive crime\Noften slips by unrecognized.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:45.22,1:41:46.89,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\Nlt was all over now.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:47.27,1:41:50.15,Default,,0,0,0,,We'd abused every rule\Nthat Vegas lived by.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:50.85,1:41:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Threatening the locals,\Nabusing the tourists,
Dialogue: 0,1:41:54.19,1:41:56.15,Default,,0,0,0,,terrifying the help.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:56.23,1:41:58.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The only chance now, l felt
Dialogue: 0,1:41:58.15,1:42:01.16,Default,,0,0,0,,was the possibility\Nthat we'd gone to such excess
Dialogue: 0,1:42:01.61,1:42:04.28,Default,,0,0,0,,that nobody in the position\Nto bring the hammer\Ndown on us
Dialogue: 0,1:42:04.37,1:42:06.16,Default,,0,0,0,,could possibly believe it.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:06.75,1:42:09.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Fifteen minutes to get\Nmy attorney to the airport,
Dialogue: 0,1:42:10.12,1:42:11.67,Default,,0,0,0,,could we make it?
Dialogue: 0,1:42:12.42,1:42:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Christ!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:15.21,1:42:16.76,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:17.67,1:42:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, fuck!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:19.01,1:42:20.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck.\NWhoa, shit! Whoa, shit!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:21.05,1:42:23.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God. Oh, God.\NYou son of a bitch !
Dialogue: 0,1:42:23.60,1:42:25.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:25.68,1:42:26.93,Default,,0,0,0,,(SCREAMING)
Dialogue: 0,1:42:26.97,1:42:29.10,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: You're going\Nthe wrong way.\NDUKE: The next left.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:29.39,1:42:30.39,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: Stop!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:30.48,1:42:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Go! Fuck!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:37.19,1:42:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Take a right here.\NTake a right here.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:48.100,1:42:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,GONZO: Goddamn it. We're lost.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:52.46,1:42:55.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What are we doing\Nout here on this\Ngodforsaken road?
Dialogue: 0,1:42:56.30,1:42:58.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The airport's over there.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:58.30,1:43:01.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn it! It's over there.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:01.97,1:43:03.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I've never\Nmissed a plane yet.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:04.30,1:43:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,(TIRES SCREECHING)
Dialogue: 0,1:43:27.28,1:43:28.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on !
Dialogue: 0,1:43:34.62,1:43:37.13,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. I'm gonna drop you\Nright next to the plane.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:37.21,1:43:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuck you. I'm gonna\Nhave to take the blame.\NThey'll crucify me.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:40.01,1:43:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Right here, right here.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:41.63,1:43:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Ridiculous, man.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:42.76,1:43:46.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Just say you were hitchhiking\Nto the airport,\Nand I picked you up.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:46.85,1:43:47.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You bastard.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:48.06,1:43:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:59.90,1:44:01.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, hey! Hey, listen.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:02.53,1:44:04.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't take any guff\Nfrom these swine.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:05.03,1:44:07.61,Default,,0,0,0,,If you have\Nany trouble, remember,
Dialogue: 0,1:44:07.82,1:44:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,you can always send a telegram\Nto the right people.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:10.08,1:44:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, explaining my position.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:12.20,1:44:14.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Some asshole wrote\Na poem about that once.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:14.87,1:44:17.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Probably good advice,\Nif you have shit for brains.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:19.46,1:44:20.88,Default,,0,0,0,,(GONZO LAUGHING)
Dialogue: 0,1:44:24.26,1:44:28.60,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING: There he goes.\NOne of God's own prototypes.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:29.43,1:44:30.93,Default,,0,0,0,,A high-powered mutant\Nof some kind
Dialogue: 0,1:44:31.02,1:44:33.22,Default,,0,0,0,,never even considered\Nfor mass production.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:33.77,1:44:35.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Too weird to live,
Dialogue: 0,1:44:35.56,1:44:37.69,Default,,0,0,0,,(GRUNTING)\Nand too rare to die.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:58.58,1:45:03.92,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) There you stood\Non the edge of your feather
Dialogue: 0,1:45:04.97,1:45:09.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Expecting to fly
Dialogue: 0,1:45:13.10,1:45:16.06,Default,,0,0,0,,DUKE NARRATING:\NWe're all wired\Ninto a survival trip now.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:16.44,1:45:18.98,Default,,0,0,0,,No more of the speed\Nthat fueled the '60s.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:19.44,1:45:22.19,Default,,0,0,0,,That was the fatal flaw\Nin Tim Leary's trip.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:22.82,1:45:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,He crashed\Naround America, selling\N"consciousness expansion"
Dialogue: 0,1:45:25.82,1:45:27.28,Default,,0,0,0,,without ever giving a thought
Dialogue: 0,1:45:27.36,1:45:29.36,Default,,0,0,0,,to the grim\Nmeat-hook realities\Nthat were lying in wait
Dialogue: 0,1:45:29.45,1:45:32.20,Default,,0,0,0,,for all those people\Nwho took him seriously.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:32.99,1:45:34.87,Default,,0,0,0,,All those pathetically\Neager acid freaks
Dialogue: 0,1:45:34.95,1:45:38.54,Default,,0,0,0,,who thought they could\Nbuy peace and understanding\Nfor three bucks a hit.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:39.25,1:45:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,But their loss and failure
Dialogue: 0,1:45:42.13,1:45:43.63,Default,,0,0,0,,is ours too.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:44.51,1:45:47.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What Leary took down with him\Nwas the central illusion\Nof a whole lifestyle
Dialogue: 0,1:45:47.63,1:45:49.18,Default,,0,0,0,,that he helped create.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:49.76,1:45:52.22,Default,,0,0,0,,A generation\Nof permanent cripples,
Dialogue: 0,1:45:52.30,1:45:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,failed seekers,
Dialogue: 0,1:45:53.97,1:45:58.02,Default,,0,0,0,,who never understood\Nthe essential old-mystic\Nfallacy of the acid culture.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:58.98,1:46:00.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The desperate assumption
Dialogue: 0,1:46:00.52,1:46:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,that somebody\Nor at least some force
Dialogue: 0,1:46:03.82,1:46:06.57,Default,,0,0,0,,is tending the light\Nat the end of the tunnel.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:13.49,1:46:15.91,Default,,0,0,0,,There was only one road\Nback to L.A.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:15.99,1:46:18.37,Default,,0,0,0,,U.S. lnterstate 1 5.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:18.45,1:46:22.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Just a flat out\Nhigh-speed burn through\NBaker and Barstow and Berdoo.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:22.84,1:46:24.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Then onto\Nthe Hollywood Freeway,
Dialogue: 0,1:46:24.17,1:46:25.46,Default,,0,0,0,,straight into\Nfrantic oblivion,
Dialogue: 0,1:46:25.55,1:46:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,safety, obscurity.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:28.22,1:46:31.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Just another freak\Nin the freak kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:31.30,1:46:36.01,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) I was born\Nin a cross-fire hurricane
Dialogue: 0,1:46:38.18,1:46:43.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But l howled at my ma\Nin the driving rain
Dialogue: 0,1:46:45.27,1:46:49.99,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's all right now
Dialogue: 0,1:46:50.07,1:46:52.28,Default,,0,0,0,,ln fact, it's a gas
Dialogue: 0,1:46:52.36,1:46:56.07,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's all right
Dialogue: 0,1:46:56.16,1:46:59.66,Default,,0,0,0,,l'm Jumpin' Jack Flash.\Nlt's a gas, gas, gas.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:09.38,1:47:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,l was raised by a toothless,\Nbearded hag
Dialogue: 0,1:47:16.72,1:47:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,l was schooled with a strap\Nright across my back
Dialogue: 0,1:47:23.73,1:47:28.48,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's all right now
Dialogue: 0,1:47:28.57,1:47:30.73,Default,,0,0,0,,ln fact, it's a gas
Dialogue: 0,1:47:30.82,1:47:34.57,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's all right
Dialogue: 0,1:47:34.66,1:47:38.45,Default,,0,0,0,,l'm Jumpin' Jack Flash.\Nlt's a gas, gas, gas
Dialogue: 0,1:48:07.40,1:48:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,l was drowned\Nl was washed up\Nand left for dead
Dialogue: 0,1:48:14.45,1:48:16.74,Default,,0,0,0,,l fell down to my feet
Dialogue: 0,1:48:16.82,1:48:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And l saw they bled
Dialogue: 0,1:48:19.95,1:48:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah\Nl frowned
Dialogue: 0,1:48:23.12,1:48:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,At the crumbs\Nof a crust of bread
Dialogue: 0,1:48:26.96,1:48:29.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah, yeah,\Nl was crowned
Dialogue: 0,1:48:30.05,1:48:33.80,Default,,0,0,0,,With a spike\Nright through my head
Dialogue: 0,1:48:33.88,1:48:35.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah, yeah
Dialogue: 0,1:48:35.30,1:48:40.18,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's all right now
Dialogue: 0,1:48:40.26,1:48:42.22,Default,,0,0,0,,ln fact, it's a gas
Dialogue: 0,1:48:42.31,1:48:46.23,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's all right
Dialogue: 0,1:48:46.31,1:48:50.19,Default,,0,0,0,,l'm Jumpin' Jack Flash.\Nlt's a gas, gas, gas
Dialogue: 0,1:48:53.57,1:49:10.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Jumpin' Jack Flash.\Nlt's a gas
Dialogue: 0,1:49:10.96,1:49:14.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Jumpin' Jack Flash.\Nlt's a gas.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:16.90,1:50:19.61,Default,,0,0,0,,(SINGING) Bright Iight city\Ngonna set my soul
Dialogue: 0,1:50:19.70,1:50:22.91,Default,,0,0,0,,lt's gonna set my soul on fire
Dialogue: 0,1:50:22.99,1:50:25.99,Default,,0,0,0,,l got a whole lotta money\Nthat's a-ready to burn
Dialogue: 0,1:50:26.08,1:50:29.16,Default,,0,0,0,,So get those stakes up high
Dialogue: 0,1:50:29.25,1:50:32.88,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a thousand\Npretty women waitin' out there
Dialogue: 0,1:50:32.96,1:50:36.00,Default,,0,0,0,,They're all waitin'\NThe devil may care
Dialogue: 0,1:50:36.09,1:50:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And l'm just a devil\Nwith love to spare
Dialogue: 0,1:50:39.26,1:50:42.59,Default,,0,0,0,,So Viva Las Vegas
Dialogue: 0,1:50:42.68,1:50:48.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Viva Las Vegas
Dialogue: 0,1:50:50.73,1:50:53.27,Default,,0,0,0,,How l wish that\Nthere were more
Dialogue: 0,1:50:53.35,1:50:56.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Than the 24 hours in the day
Dialogue: 0,1:50:57.02,1:50:59.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if l ran out of sleep
Dialogue: 0,1:50:59.74,1:51:02.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, l wouldn't\Nsleep a minute away
Dialogue: 0,1:51:02.78,1:51:06.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, there's blackjack\Nand poker\Nand the roulette wheel
Dialogue: 0,1:51:06.37,1:51:09.66,Default,,0,0,0,,A fortune won and lost\Non every deal
Dialogue: 0,1:51:09.75,1:51:12.54,Default,,0,0,0,,All you need's a strong heart\Nand nerves of steel
Dialogue: 0,1:51:12.62,1:51:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,So Viva Las Vegas
Dialogue: 0,1:51:16.25,1:51:22.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Viva Las Vegas
Dialogue: 0,1:51:22.47,1:51:25.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Viva Las Vegas\Nwhere the neon signs\Nare flashing
Dialogue: 0,1:51:25.43,1:51:27.35,Default,,0,0,0,,And the one-armed\Nbandits crashing
Dialogue: 0,1:51:27.43,1:51:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,All those hopes\Ndown the drain
Dialogue: 0,1:51:30.27,1:51:33.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Viva Las Vegas\Nturning day into nighttime
Dialogue: 0,1:51:33.23,1:51:34.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Turning night into daytime
Dialogue: 0,1:51:34.98,1:51:39.15,Default,,0,0,0,,lf you see it once\Nyou'll never be the same again
Dialogue: 0,1:51:41.07,1:51:44.07,Default,,0,0,0,,l gotta keep on runnin'\NGonna have me some fun
Dialogue: 0,1:51:44.16,1:51:47.28,Default,,0,0,0,,lf it costs me\Nmy very last dime
Dialogue: 0,1:51:47.37,1:51:50.41,Default,,0,0,0,,lf l wind up broke\Nthen l'll always remember
Dialogue: 0,1:51:50.49,1:51:53.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That l had a swingin' time
Dialogue: 0,1:51:53.33,1:51:56.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, l'm gonna give it\Neverything l've got
Dialogue: 0,1:51:57.04,1:52:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Lady Luck's with me,\NDice, stay hot
Dialogue: 0,1:52:00.09,1:52:02.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Got coke up my nose\Nto dry away the snot
Dialogue: 0,1:52:03.05,1:52:06.43,Default,,0,0,0,,So Viva Las Vegas
Dialogue: 0,1:52:06.51,1:52:12.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Viva Las Vegas
Dialogue: 0,1:52:12.77,1:52:15.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Viva, Viva
Dialogue: 0,1:52:15.52,1:52:20.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Las Vegas
Dialogue: 0,1:52:20.78,1:52:22.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Whee!
